Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.14,0:00:09.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[drums playing]
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.49,0:00:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[ {\i1}Mission: Impossible{\i0}\Ntheme playing]
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.80,0:00:21.93,Default,,0,0,0,,[music stops]
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.55,0:00:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] {\i1}We live and die{\i0}\N{\i1}in the shadows,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.90,0:00:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for those we hold close{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.20,0:00:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and for those we never meet.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.43,0:00:36.78,Default,,0,0,0,,[Solomon Lane] {\i1}The end you {\i0}\N{\i1}always feared is coming.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.95,0:00:38.87,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}The Anti-God.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.04,0:00:41.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[NSA representative]\N{\i1}This "entity" has{\i0} {\i1}multiple personalities.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.26,0:00:43.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[Denlinger] {\i1}You’re{\i0}\N{\i1}telling me this thing{\i0} {\i1}has a mind of its own?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.26,0:00:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}A self-aware, {\i0}\N{\i1}self-learning, {\i0} {\i1}truth-eating digital parasite{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.13,0:00:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}infesting all of cyberspace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.31,0:00:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[Denlinger] {\i1}An enemy that {\i0}\N{\i1}is everywhere and nowhere {\i0} {\i1}and has no center.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.14,0:00:53.01,Default,,0,0,0,,[NSA representative] {\i1}Patiently {\i0}\N{\i1}listening, reading, watching.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.18,0:00:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,[NRO representative]\N{\i1}Harvesting our deepest {\i0} {\i1}personal secrets for years.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.06,0:00:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[DIA representative] {\i1}Able to {\i0}\N{\i1}beguile, blackmail, bribe {\i0} {\i1}or be anyone it wants.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.84,0:01:01.97,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}Ethan, that is not me! {\i0}\N{\i1}You’re talking to the Entity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.15,0:01:04.98,Default,,0,0,0,,[Kittridge] {\i1}Whoever controls {\i0}\N{\i1}the Entity controls the truth.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.15,0:01:07.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[NSA representative]\N{\i1}...most secure data centers {\i0} {\i1}are breached and corrupted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.89,0:01:09.28,Default,,0,0,0,,[JSOC representative]\N{\i1}The Entity will know precisely{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.46,0:01:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}how to undermine{\i0}\N{\i1}our every strength.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.07,0:01:12.51,Default,,0,0,0,,[DIA representative] {\i1}Turn {\i0}\N{\i1}our allies into enemies...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.68,0:01:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[JSOC representative]\N{\i1}And exploit our every weakness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.42,0:01:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[DIA representative] {\i1}...and {\i0}\N{\i1}our enemies into aggressors.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.99,0:01:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}An unstoppable force {\i0}\N{\i1}of destructive power that would {\i0} {\i1}just lay waste to everything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.30,0:01:24.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[White Widow] {\i1}The world is {\i0}\N{\i1}changing. Truth is vanishing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.78,0:01:26.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}War is coming.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.07,0:01:54.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[Erika on recording]\N{\i1}Good evening, Ethan.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.90,0:01:56.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is your president.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.46,0:01:59.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Since you won’t reply{\i0}\N{\i1}to anyone else,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.47,0:02:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought{\i0}\N{\i1}I’d reach out directly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.17,0:02:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}First, I want to thank you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.25,0:02:07.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for a lifetime of devoted {\i0}\N{\i1}and unrelenting service.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.65,0:02:15.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Were it not for{\i0}\N{\i1}the tireless dedication{\i0} {\i1}of you and your team,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.66,0:02:18.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the Earth would be{\i0}\N{\i1}a very different place.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.79,0:02:22.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It might not{\i0}\N{\i1}even be here at all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.27,0:02:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Every risk you’ve taken...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.80,0:02:30.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}every comrade you’ve lost {\i0}\N{\i1}in the field...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.42,0:02:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}every personal sacrifice{\i0}\N{\i1}you made...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.42,0:02:43.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}has brought this world{\i0}\N{\i1}another sunrise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.38,0:02:50.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It’s been 35 years{\i0}\N{\i1}since circumstances{\i0} {\i1}brought you to us{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.65,0:02:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you were given the choice,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.39,0:02:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}since the IMF saved you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.70,0:02:58.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from a life in prison.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.57,0:03:02.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And though you{\i0}\N{\i1}never followed orders,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.75,0:03:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you never let us down.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.01,0:03:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[no audible dialogue]
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.88,0:03:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,[sentimental music playing]
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.03,0:03:25.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You were always{\i0}\N{\i1}the best of men...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.21,0:03:29.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in the worst of times.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.56,0:03:34.13,Default,,0,0,0,,[no audible dialogue]
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.22,0:03:39.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I need you to be that man now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.74,0:03:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In the months since you {\i0}\N{\i1}evaded capture in Austria,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.31,0:03:47.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}every corner of cyberspace {\i0}\N{\i1}has been infested {\i0} {\i1}by the truth-eating,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.40,0:03:50.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}parasitic A.I. known{\i0}\N{\i1}to us as the Entity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.10,0:03:52.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Under its influence,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.67,0:03:55.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}digital information {\i0}\N{\i1}has been corrupted worldwide.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.89,0:03:58.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nations and people no longer {\i0}\N{\i1}know what to believe.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.11,0:04:00.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Antagonism,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.72,0:04:03.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}aggression and martial law {\i0}\N{\i1}are the new world order.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.07,0:04:06.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Exploiting this{\i0}\N{\i1}paranoid atmosphere,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.33,0:04:08.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the Entity has inspired{\i0}\N{\i1}a doomsday cult{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.07,0:04:11.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with acolytes devoted to {\i0}\N{\i1}ridding the world of corruption{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.03,0:04:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}through human extinction.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.12,0:04:15.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And He said unto Noah,{\i0}\N{\i1}"Behold..."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.78,0:04:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"I will bring a flood{\i0}\N{\i1}upon the earth{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.08,0:04:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to destroy all flesh."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.91,0:04:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The children of the atom {\i0}\N{\i1}shall rise from the ashes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.13,0:04:23.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the Entity will{\i0}\N{\i1}help them rebuild.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.52,0:04:27.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[Erika] {\i1}These fanatics {\i0}\N{\i1}are secretly infiltrating {\i0} {\i1}every level of law enforcement,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.83,0:04:30.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}government and our military,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.27,0:04:33.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}devoted to serving their {\i0}\N{\i1}digital master’s ultimate goal.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.49,0:04:36.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our only hope of{\i0}\N{\i1}controlling the Entity{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.10,0:04:40.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}relies on finding {\i0}\N{\i1}its original source code.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.32,0:04:44.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If anyone knows the whereabouts {\i0}\N{\i1}of this code, it’s this man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.46,0:04:48.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}His identity, his past,{\i0}\N{\i1}his very existence{\i0} {\i1}have been erased,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.85,0:04:53.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}suggesting he is or was {\i0}\N{\i1}in league with the Entity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.86,0:04:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Austrian authorities have {\i0}\N{\i1}his accomplice in custody.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.47,0:05:00.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But she has refused{\i0}\N{\i1}to tell us anything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.39,0:05:03.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which brings us back to you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.65,0:05:07.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are in possession{\i0}\N{\i1}of a key believed{\i0} {\i1}to be a vital component{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.96,0:05:10.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in our struggle to acquire {\i0}\N{\i1}the Entity’s source code.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.01,0:05:13.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yet you refuse to come in,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.23,0:05:16.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}fearing any government will {\i0}\N{\i1}weaponize this malicious A.I.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.62,0:05:18.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}against the rest of the world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.93,0:05:21.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Instead you’ve resolved{\i0}\N{\i1}to kill the Entity,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.36,0:05:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a reckless act that {\i0}\N{\i1}would trigger the total {\i0} {\i1}annihilation of cyberspace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.72,0:05:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This would eradicate{\i0}\N{\i1}the global economy,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.20,0:05:32.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}plunging the world into war {\i0}\N{\i1}and famine without end.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.38,0:05:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Agent Hunt. Ethan.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.90,0:05:38.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please surrender.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.21,0:05:41.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or the blood of the world {\i0}\N{\i1}will be on your hands.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.82,0:05:46.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This message will {\i0}\N{\i1}self-destruct in five seconds.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.82,0:05:48.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come home, Ethan,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.09,0:05:51.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and bring us that key.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.88,0:06:05.40,Default,,0,0,0,,[crowd chanting]\NEnd it now! End it now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.58,0:06:08.67,Default,,0,0,0,,End it now!\NEnd it now! End it now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.85,0:06:11.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[chanting continues]\N[dogs barking]
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.07,0:06:16.12,Default,,0,0,0,,[plane whirs]
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.90,0:06:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,End it now!\NEnd it now! End it now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.17,0:06:34.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[chanting continues]
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.07,0:06:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,[brakes squeal]
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.75,0:07:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.75,0:07:29.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Luther.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.49,0:07:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] Sorry about the decor.\NThe Ritz was booked solid.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.28,0:07:35.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, some drapes,\Na few throw pillows, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.24,0:07:36.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, a minibar.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.28,0:07:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Foosball table.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.03,0:07:42.42,Default,,0,0,0,,[all chuckle]
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.12,0:07:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, bro.\NHey.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.91,0:07:57.78,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s always good to see you\Non the right side of the grass.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.39,0:08:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m worried you’re\Nworking too hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.39,0:08:04.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t worry about ol’ Luther.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.44,0:08:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.14,0:08:08.71,Default,,0,0,0,,So, what did you\Nmanage to find out?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.05,0:08:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,A lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.84,0:08:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,More than I bargained for.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.45,0:08:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,So, what’s the play?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.19,0:08:19.15,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] First,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.32,0:08:21.28,Default,,0,0,0,,we have to find Gabriel.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.46,0:08:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] How do we find him?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.43,0:08:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You will betray us
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.04,0:08:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,because he spared your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.04,0:08:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.22,0:08:44.26,Default,,0,0,0,,[gunfire]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.72,0:09:04.94,Default,,0,0,0,,[electrical crackling]\N[pained grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.20,0:09:07.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting, straining]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.90,0:09:10.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.42,0:09:13.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[electrical crackling]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.08,0:09:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.51,0:09:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,[crackling]\N[groaning]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.38,0:09:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting, straining]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.17,0:09:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,[gunshots]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.23,0:09:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] STOP. STOP.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.62,0:09:37.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouting in French]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.40,0:09:38.40,Default,,0,0,0,,[in English]\NWait, wait, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.58,0:09:40.15,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks French]
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.58,0:09:43.36,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers in French] Why...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.54,0:09:45.98,Default,,0,0,0,,did you spare my life?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.46,0:09:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,[in English]\NWait, wait, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.37,0:09:54.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You call that in, it’s the end\Nof the world-- simple as that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.90,0:09:55.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Degas, isn’t it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.07,0:09:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Clock is running.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.12,0:10:00.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You take us in,\Nthere won’t be anyone on Earth who can stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.60,0:10:02.08,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s a part of\Nyou that knows that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.25,0:10:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I can see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.21,0:10:04.78,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans]
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.95,0:10:06.43,Default,,0,0,0,,For God’s sake,\Njust trust him! Wait, wait, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.61,0:10:08.13,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s okay, it’s okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.30,0:10:10.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Degas, it’s okay.\NThere’s no nations on this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.78,0:10:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s no rival\Nideologies, no dogma.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.83,0:10:16.14,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s who keeps their head\Nand who panics.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.31,0:10:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The Entity wants you scared,\Nit wants us all scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.40,0:10:21.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It wants us divided.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.27,0:10:23.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It wants you to turn us in.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.75,0:10:25.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.37,0:10:31.76,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s gonna be okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.33,0:10:33.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Degas.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.46,0:10:36.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.51,0:10:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,[sniffs]
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.84,0:11:08.41,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispering]\NWe’re friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.28,0:11:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,[both sigh]
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.98,0:11:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] Gabriel...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.98,0:11:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.99,0:11:26.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[classical string music plays]
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.99,0:11:31.99,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}You shouldn’t be{\i0}\N{\i1}in there without backup.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.17,0:11:34.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] {\i1}Benji, please.{\i0}\N{\i1}We got this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.26,0:11:36.61,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] This is\Na terrible idea. {\i1}Just relax.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.78,0:11:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan, this place is crawling\Nwith clandestine services.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.00,0:11:40.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should get out of there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.48,0:11:42.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I see them. It’s okay.\NStay calm, Benji.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.14,0:11:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t think Gabriel would\Nrisk coming to that party.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.53,0:11:46.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Abort.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.14,0:11:50.32,Default,,0,0,0,,No, let’s just hold\Nour nerve. He’s here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.49,0:11:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s got to be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.41,0:11:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan, for God’s sake, abort!\N{\i1}We’ll figure this out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.54,0:11:56.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Not a problem yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.72,0:12:03.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[security] Stay where you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.55,0:12:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t move, Hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.29,0:12:12.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sure it’s really me?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.74,0:12:19.18,Default,,0,0,0,,All units, we have Hunt.\NI repeat, we have Hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.35,0:12:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,They can’t hear you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.92,0:12:28.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Grace.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.23,0:12:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[inhales sharply]
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.79,0:12:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,[classical music continues]
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.45,0:12:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn’t even see\Nyou get that one.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.20,0:12:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What separates a good\Npickpocket from a great one?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.37,0:12:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Timing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.72,0:12:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.12,0:12:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice and slow.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.44,0:13:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing personal.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.96,0:13:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,[thuds]
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.36,0:13:16.36,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, I like\Nthe longer hair.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.53,0:13:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I really appreciate\Nyour coming, but you shouldn’t be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.84,0:13:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn’t have much choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.28,0:13:23.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you expect\Nme to betray him?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.80,0:13:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I expect you to\Nsave him from himself
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.02,0:13:29.20,Default,,0,0,0,,and the world from him.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.55,0:13:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs] Kittridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.68,0:13:36.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You just bought yourself\Na world of trouble, Grace.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.64,0:13:38.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The whole world’s\Nin trouble, Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.77,0:13:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re the only one\NI trust to save it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.39,0:13:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,So, what’s the play?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.65,0:13:51.30,Default,,0,0,0,,[all grunting]\N[electrical zap]
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.48,0:13:52.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Grace!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.70,0:13:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,[straining]\N[electrical zap]
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.14,0:13:56.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Grace.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.62,0:14:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Gabriel’s got a job\Nfor you, Hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.63,0:14:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[clicks]
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.76,0:14:06.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] {\i1}Ethan, wake up!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.89,0:14:08.76,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping]
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.98,0:14:12.33,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] Okay, what do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.59,0:14:15.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me you have a plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.16,0:14:21.60,Default,,0,0,0,,They took my watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.77,0:14:24.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Your watch?\NYeah, and my cuff links.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.69,0:14:26.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Had lock picks in them.\NI see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.91,0:14:29.09,Default,,0,0,0,,We’ll find a way out,\Nokay? Now, listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.26,0:14:30.26,Default,,0,0,0,,[thud upstairs]
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.87,0:14:34.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, it’s too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.66,0:14:36.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.96,0:14:39.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, Grace, look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.88,0:14:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re gonna get through this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.14,0:14:45.32,Default,,0,0,0,,[breathing heavily]\NGet through what?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.49,0:14:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Just keep telling yourself...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.32,0:14:49.36,Default,,0,0,0,,it’s only pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.54,0:14:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,[door creaks]
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.46,0:14:56.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]\N[blow lands]
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.20,0:14:58.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop!\N[Gabriel] Don’t touch him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.29,0:15:02.86,Default,,0,0,0,,You can’t hurt him.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.03,0:15:04.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.08,0:15:07.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.73,0:15:11.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Take you back to Shanghai?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.00,0:15:13.09,Default,,0,0,0,,What was her name?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.09,0:15:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Julia!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.74,0:15:17.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The former Mrs. Hunt.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.92,0:15:19.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Did Ethan fail to mention her?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.75,0:15:22.88,Default,,0,0,0,,A fellow named\NDavian took her...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.92,0:15:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,and ransomed her for something
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.40,0:15:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,only Ethan could get.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.93,0:15:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Davian called it{\i0}\N{\i1}the Rabbit’s Foot.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.58,0:15:33.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it had another name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.54,0:15:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The Anti-God.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.24,0:15:40.11,Default,,0,0,0,,They never told you what was\Nin that canister, did they?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.29,0:15:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But you always wondered.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.42,0:15:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Stealing the Rabbit’s Foot\Nwas just one event
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.77,0:15:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,in a lifelong pattern,\Nrepeating itself over and over.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.47,0:15:54.78,Default,,0,0,0,,For every life\Nhe’s tried to save, he’s gambled millions more,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.95,0:15:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,doubling down and down again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.04,0:16:01.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And now the fate of every\Nliving soul on Earth is
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.26,0:16:03.61,Default,,0,0,0,,his responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.79,0:16:06.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You must be exhausted.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.79,0:16:08.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Where’s the key?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.58,0:16:10.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Let her go.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.23,0:16:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we’ll discuss it.\NWe don’t have the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.88,0:16:15.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone you hold\Nclose will die tonight
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.15,0:16:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,for the sake of those\Nyou will never meet,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.02,0:16:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,unless you do exactly as I say.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.81,0:16:24.42,Default,,0,0,0,,He also said the key would\Nbe his on the train, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.12,0:16:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You had one job:
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.90,0:16:32.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Get on the train, get the key, {\i0}\N{\i1}get off the train.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.25,0:16:36.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How did your master{\i0}\N{\i1}take the news when it{\i0} {\i1}found out you blew it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.60,0:16:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,You failed,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.21,0:16:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,and now the Entity\Nhas forsaken you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.09,0:16:44.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Your team’s been\Ncompromised, Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.39,0:16:48.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I know what Luther’s doing.\NI know what you’re planning.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.36,0:16:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Resist me\Nand I’ll make you pay dearly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.84,0:16:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,If you cooperate,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.40,0:16:54.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I can help.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.27,0:16:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,In exchange for what?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.45,0:16:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re searching for\Na Russian submarine vanished on its maiden voyage.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.89,0:17:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] The K559 {\i1}Sevastopol.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.59,0:17:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,A state-of-the-art submarine\Ncompletely undetectable to any known sonar.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.55,0:17:09.64,Default,,0,0,0,,And the secret to\Nits invisibility was that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.81,0:17:11.16,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] The Podkova.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.33,0:17:13.20,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}A counter-acoustic {\i0}\N{\i1}algorithmic drive{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.38,0:17:16.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}located in the{\i0}Sevastopol’s\N{\i1}sonar sphere.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.21,0:17:18.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, in the winter of 2012
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.56,0:17:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the Russians discovered\Na computer virus of unknown origin
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.17,0:17:22.91,Default,,0,0,0,,spreading through\Ntheir Black Sea fleet.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.09,0:17:25.75,Default,,0,0,0,,A digital covert operative.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.91,0:17:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,We suspect this mystery virus\Nwas only intended
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.26,0:17:31.87,Default,,0,0,0,,to sabotage the Podkova,\Nrendering the submarine detectable.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.05,0:17:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead...\NIt tricked the crew
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.97,0:17:35.71,Default,,0,0,0,,into sinking themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.88,0:17:37.93,Default,,0,0,0,,[Russian officer] Captain! Our\Nown torpedo is not responding.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.10,0:17:39.36,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s coming right at us!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.54,0:17:41.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Our torpedo’s homing!\NRange 400 meters!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.54,0:17:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Sound the collision alar--
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.54,0:17:48.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] If we’re right,\Nthe one thing we need to kill the Entity,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.55,0:17:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}its original source code,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.24,0:17:53.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is buried in the{\i0}Sevastopol’s\N{\i1}sonar sphere.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.77,0:17:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}Somewhere deep {\i0}\N{\i1}at the bottom of the ocean, {\i0} {\i1}frozen in time,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.64,0:18:00.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}where even the Entity{\i0}\N{\i1}can’t reach it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.47,0:18:04.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, the Podkova’s housing {\i0}\N{\i1}was designed to self-destruct {\i0} {\i1}if tampered with.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.74,0:18:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,The only way to\Nsafely open it...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.61,0:18:11.14,Default,,0,0,0,,is with a specially designed\Ncruciform key.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.31,0:18:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] {\i1}The two halves {\i0}\N{\i1}of which were held by the{\i0} {\i1}Sevastopol’s {\i0}{\i1}captain and XO.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.01,0:18:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel] {\i1}They were pulled {\i0}\N{\i1}from the drifting pack ice{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.40,0:18:20.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in the spring of 2012{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.36,0:18:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}by Inuit fishermen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.80,0:18:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A man of your skills{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.76,0:18:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,now has all he needs\Nto pinpoint that sub down to the square yard.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.59,0:18:34.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You think I’m gonna\Nget the source code and bring it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.68,0:18:36.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t think. I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.42,0:18:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m gonna let you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.64,0:18:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you’re gonna find\Nthe Entity’s source code and bring it to me
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.43,0:18:44.52,Default,,0,0,0,,in exchange for Grace.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.69,0:18:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I’ll take control\Nof the Entity,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.08,0:18:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,the proverbial genie\Nyou let out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.43,0:18:53.26,Default,,0,0,0,,The Rabbit’s Foot.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.44,0:18:55.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The Anti-God.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.22,0:18:56.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel]\NIt wasn’t a biological or a chemical weapon
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.14,0:18:58.88,Default,,0,0,0,,you took from Shanghai.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.05,0:19:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The vial you traded for Julia {\i0}\N{\i1}contained malicious code.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.79,0:19:05.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The primordial digital ooze
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.58,0:19:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,from which a weapon evolved.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.19,0:19:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,A weapon the East\Ncouldn’t make work.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.76,0:19:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,A weapon the West might never\Nhave made on their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.98,0:19:15.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You didn’t know\Nwhat you were stealing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.02,0:19:17.28,Default,,0,0,0,,None of us did.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.46,0:19:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew why I was stealing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.33,0:19:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,They kidnapped my wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.38,0:19:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Stealing the Rabbit’s Foot {\i0}\N{\i1}was the only way {\i0} {\i1}I could get her back.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.34,0:19:28.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I sank that submarine\Nas much as the Entity did.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.12,0:19:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Without you, Ethan,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.69,0:19:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,there’d be no Entity.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.17,0:19:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you don’t find that sub\Nin the next few days...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.65,0:19:41.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s the end of the world\Nas we know it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.18,0:19:43.57,Default,,0,0,0,,And it will all be his fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.57,0:19:46.14,Default,,0,0,0,,He knows it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.32,0:19:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.40,0:19:50.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me I’m wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.63,0:19:54.15,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales]
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.59,0:20:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] False tooth.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.55,0:20:04.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Cyanide capsule.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.29,0:20:09.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I bite down on this,\Nand I’m dead in sixty seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.12,0:20:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You’ll never see\Nthat source code.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.56,0:20:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t touch him!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.82,0:20:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Spit it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.13,0:20:16.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Release her first.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.74,0:20:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You won’t do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.04,0:20:19.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I got nothing to lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.91,0:20:21.26,Default,,0,0,0,,But Grace does.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.09,0:20:23.92,Default,,0,0,0,,And with you dead,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.09,0:20:26.44,Default,,0,0,0,,who’s gonna save her?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.62,0:20:29.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Spit it out.\NEthan.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.49,0:20:33.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember, Grace,\Nit’s only pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.93,0:20:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Medic!Ethan!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.72,0:20:40.11,Default,,0,0,0,,[gagging]
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.37,0:20:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,[medic]\NBring the defibrillator!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.68,0:20:44.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.11,0:20:46.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.29,0:20:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, wait! Charging.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.73,0:20:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Charging.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.21,0:20:51.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.55,0:20:52.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.56,0:20:54.52,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans]
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.56,0:20:59.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] Keys!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.26,0:21:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.09,0:21:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,[chains rattling]\N[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.66,0:21:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel] I need him alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.88,0:21:11.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Kill her.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.93,0:21:16.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Gabriel’s getting away.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.76,0:21:19.85,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts] Go.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.84,0:21:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]\N[Grace shouts]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.11,0:21:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,[both grunting]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.24,0:21:29.94,Default,,0,0,0,,[gunfire]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.11,0:21:31.76,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting, straining]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.99,0:21:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,[glass breaks]\N[both grunting]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.60,0:21:43.60,Default,,0,0,0,,[both grunting]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.26,0:21:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting, gasping]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.96,0:21:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] Ethan!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.44,0:21:55.92,Default,,0,0,0,,[strained yell]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.53,0:21:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,[all grunting]
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.62,0:22:03.54,Default,,0,0,0,,[blows landing]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.98,0:22:06.29,Default,,0,0,0,,[assailant yells]\N[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.80,0:22:09.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting,\Nyelling continues]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.89,0:22:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,[blows landing]\N[items shattering]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.12,0:22:17.51,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan grunts]\N[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.68,0:22:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.03,0:22:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[metallic clank]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.17,0:22:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.35,0:22:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Gabriel’s getting away.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.35,0:22:33.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Grace.[whimpers]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.22,0:22:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa. Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.18,0:22:37.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You don’t think that\NI would have let them...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.23,0:22:40.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Grace, I would never let\Nanything happen to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.23,0:22:41.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.84,0:22:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean--
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.02,0:22:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Wha--
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.19,0:22:48.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean--
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.72,0:22:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, they were gonna kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.72,0:22:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\NYeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.02,0:22:53.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.89,0:22:56.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you did great,\Nby the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.64,0:22:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,We really got to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.55,0:23:05.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[ {\i1}Mission: Impossible{\i0}\Ntheme playing]
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.04,0:23:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,[song ends]
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.05,0:24:06.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Freeze!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.05,0:24:08.53,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting]
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.32,0:24:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I got him!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.54,0:24:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,We talked about this.\NEthan wants him alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.41,0:24:19.28,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] I want him dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.42,0:24:21.68,Default,,0,0,0,,She’ll be the death of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.34,0:24:35.38,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.62,0:24:52.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.14,0:24:55.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.11,0:25:05.20,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan in French] What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.37,0:25:07.55,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s how he spoke to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.64,0:25:11.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[electronic beep]
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.89,0:25:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,[metallic click]
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.48,0:26:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re not seriously gonna...?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.61,0:26:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] It will change you.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:27.11,0:26:29.11,Default,,0,0,0,,[clicks, hisses]
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.12,0:26:36.08,Default,,0,0,0,,[thuds]
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.25,0:26:38.43,Default,,0,0,0,,[labored breaths]
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.69,0:26:42.04,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, I’m here.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.21,0:26:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Now what do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.91,0:26:46.43,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.30,0:26:51.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice]\N{\i1}Good evening, Mr. Hunt.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.74,0:26:53.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have questions.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.74,0:26:57.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Entity has answers.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.49,0:26:59.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But you have to let it in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.97,0:27:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,[strained grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.19,0:27:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[electrical zapping]
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.62,0:27:07.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice]\N{\i1}You know this place.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.89,0:27:10.94,Default,,0,0,0,,[labored breaths]
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.11,0:27:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is only{\i0}\N{\i1}pain if you resist.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.94,0:27:15.51,Default,,0,0,0,,[pained grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.68,0:27:18.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[electrical zapping]
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.25,0:27:20.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Again,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.77,0:27:22.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you know this place.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.77,0:27:26.08,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] The Doomsday Vault.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.65,0:27:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,South Africa.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.99,0:27:30.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will meet{\i0}\N{\i1}the Entity there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.52,0:27:31.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will let it in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.13,0:27:36.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the fate of every {\i0}\N{\i1}living thing will be decided{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.18,0:27:38.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in the blink of an eye.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.57,0:27:41.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is your calling,{\i0}\N{\i1}your destiny.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.14,0:27:43.32,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] I don’t accept that.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.49,0:27:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[electrical zapping]\N[pained grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.01,0:27:50.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice] {\i1}In here,{\i0}\N{\i1}you have no secrets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.89,0:27:53.41,Default,,0,0,0,,[electrical zapping]\N[pained grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.02,0:27:58.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}The K559{\i0}Sevastopol.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.55,0:27:59.64,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] {\i1}The Podkova.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.81,0:28:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}A cruciform key.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.33,0:28:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] {\i1}My magnum opus.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.64,0:28:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,The algorithm on that drive,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.03,0:28:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,when paired with\Nthe Entity’s source code,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.60,0:28:10.99,Default,,0,0,0,,will act as the poison pill\Nyou asked for.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.17,0:28:13.74,Default,,0,0,0,,[pained grunts]
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.91,0:28:17.35,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice] {\i1}You plan{\i0}\N{\i1}to retrieve the Podkova{\i0} {\i1}from the{\i0}Sevastopol
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.52,0:28:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and destroy the Entity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.70,0:28:21.35,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] And that scares you.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.53,0:28:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice] {\i1}The Entity sees {\i0}\N{\i1}infinite possibilities.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.92,0:28:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Retrieve the Podkova{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.84,0:28:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you risk everything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.66,0:28:30.57,Default,,0,0,0,,[muffled explosion]
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.75,0:28:31.93,Default,,0,0,0,,[pained grunt]
Dialogue: 0,0:28:32.10,0:28:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,[no audible dialogue]
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.19,0:28:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,[explosion]
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.55,0:28:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice] {\i1}You will go{\i0}\N{\i1}to the Doomsday Vault{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.16,0:28:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and let the Entity in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.55,0:28:48.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is written.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.16,0:28:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] Never.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.47,0:28:52.52,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice]\N{\i1}The end is coming, Ethan.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.69,0:28:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have always known this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.17,0:28:58.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Entity offers hope{\i0}\N{\i1}for the future.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.56,0:29:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The few who survive{\i0}\N{\i1}will be stronger.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.39,0:29:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The children of the atom {\i0}\N{\i1}shall rise from the ashes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.09,0:29:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the Entity{\i0}\N{\i1}will help them rebuild.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.75,0:29:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,[in English]\N{\i1}But only if you let it in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.70,0:29:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] And if I don’t...\Nwhat then?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.23,0:29:16.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy the world\Nand you just destroy yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.32,0:29:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice]\N{\i1}The choice is yours.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.63,0:29:20.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Entity’s future{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.37,0:29:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or no future at all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.33,0:29:24.51,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan]\NLet the world be enslaved
Dialogue: 0,0:29:24.68,0:29:27.60,Default,,0,0,0,,or let the world be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:27.77,0:29:30.60,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice]\N{\i1}Now you are the chosen one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.77,0:29:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Gabriel is outcast.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.82,0:29:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He has taken steps {\i0}\N{\i1}to gain control of the Entity, {\i0} {\i1}as you will see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.30,0:29:43.04,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel] {\i1}Resist me {\i0}\N{\i1}and I’ll make you pay dearly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.26,0:29:47.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Someone you hold{\i0}\N{\i1}close will die tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.44,0:29:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] Luther.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.53,0:29:55.14,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep voice] {\i1}You know {\i0}\N{\i1}what humanity must do {\i0} {\i1}to change their destiny.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.32,0:29:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know they cannot{\i0}\N{\i1}stop the inevitable.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.15,0:30:02.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They will destroy themselves {\i0}\N{\i1}believing they have no choice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.63,0:30:06.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Their time has come.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.59,0:30:07.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In four days,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.15,0:30:10.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}they will face{\i0}\N{\i1}their final reckoning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.85,0:30:15.94,Default,,0,0,0,,[whirring, electrical zapping]
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.12,0:30:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,[suspenseful music playing]
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.60,0:31:01.52,Default,,0,0,0,,[suspenseful music intensifies]
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.79,0:31:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,[no audible dialogue]
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.79,0:31:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,[muffled] Is this real?\NIs this real?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.44,0:31:21.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.58,0:31:23.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you real? You’re real.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.58,0:31:24.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re real.\NYeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.93,0:31:26.32,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting]
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.23,0:31:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It knows.\N[Benji] It knows what?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.24,0:31:32.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I need a pen.\NSomething to write on.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:32.54,0:31:34.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You’ll take the team.\NYou’ll take them north.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.02,0:31:36.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] North? North where?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.85,0:31:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The {\i1}Sevastopol.{\i0}\NThe {\i1}Sevastopol?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.72,0:31:41.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to get caught. It’s\Nthe only way I could get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:41.77,0:31:43.21,Default,,0,0,0,,VHF receiver.\NDecompression chamber.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.38,0:31:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Steal a plane. An old plane.\NNo transponder, no GPS.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.56,0:31:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything is analog.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.12,0:31:49.25,Default,,0,0,0,,A DC-3.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.43,0:31:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything you need\Nis right in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:51.43,0:31:53.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember to transmit\Nthe coordinates every two hours for 15 minutes
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.39,0:31:55.09,Default,,0,0,0,,and I’ll listen when I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.26,0:31:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re team leader now.\NNo, I--
Dialogue: 0,0:31:57.57,0:31:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Benj, take care of your team.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:59.27,0:32:00.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Key.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.44,0:32:02.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You stay off the ice.\NWhat ice?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:02.40,0:32:04.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Just please, whatever you do,\Nno matter what, stay off the ice.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.84,0:32:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. Okay. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.10,0:32:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Go.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.84,0:32:14.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:14.32,0:32:15.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Luther.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.42,0:33:05.07,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting]
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.03,0:33:11.99,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping]
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.32,0:33:40.41,Default,,0,0,0,,[gate slams]\N[chain rattles]
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.98,0:33:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel] Tell Ethan...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:51.99,0:33:53.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ll be waiting for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.71,0:34:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,[beeping]
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.03,0:34:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping, panting]
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.90,0:34:38.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Luther.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.16,0:34:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.38,0:34:42.69,Default,,0,0,0,,How’d it go with Gabriel?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:43.95,0:34:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it went well. We...
Dialogue: 0,0:34:46.61,0:34:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You don’t say.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.22,0:34:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And so, whose blood is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.13,0:34:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:52.44,0:34:55.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, it’s no one we know.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.70,0:34:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that what I think it is?\NNothing special.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:58.14,0:35:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Plutonium core.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.36,0:35:03.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m guessing a five\Nor six megaton yield.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.62,0:35:06.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Enough to turn this entire city\Ninto a glass ashtray.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.45,0:35:08.15,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.32,0:35:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,not good.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.24,0:35:12.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[metal clanks]
Dialogue: 0,0:35:12.41,0:35:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Already tried. Can’t open it.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.68,0:35:16.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I see that.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.77,0:35:18.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Gabriel has the poison pill.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.12,0:35:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You might want to find him.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.68,0:35:23.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we will.\NCan you disarm that?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.82,0:35:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I just have to stop\Nthese nine detonators from imploding the core.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.34,0:35:30.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Detach one detonator,\Nno implosion.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.61,0:35:33.66,Default,,0,0,0,,And no implosion,\Nno critical mass.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.83,0:35:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And no critical mass,\Nno six megaton blast.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.14,0:35:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,How much time we have?\NEnough time for you to get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.36,0:35:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe with those tools\NI get these hinges off.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.36,0:35:45.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if you could\Nget that gate open,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.71,0:35:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I still have to\Ndetach one detonator.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:51.54,0:35:52.54,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.20,0:35:56.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I can save the city...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:57.59,0:36:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,but this entire network of\Ntunnels is going to cave in.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.82,0:36:10.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoever detaches\Nthat detonator...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:14.22,0:36:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,is going to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.00,0:36:18.53,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re both on the right side\Nof that gate
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.13,0:36:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,and you know it.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.14,0:36:23.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Luther, throw me the tool bag.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.66,0:36:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,They weren’t left here by\Naccident, Ethan. You know why.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.28,0:36:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Gabriel needs me alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.02,0:36:37.98,Default,,0,0,0,,And he needs you to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.15,0:36:40.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Because you are\Nthe only one who can make another poison pill.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.98,0:36:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,And I am the only one\Nwho can get to that submarine.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.81,0:36:45.99,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel] {\i1}Tell Ethan...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.73,0:36:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ll be waiting for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.29,0:36:49.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] {\i1}If he has{\i0}\N{\i1}the poison pill,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.95,0:36:52.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to bring him the Podkova
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.39,0:36:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,so he can control the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:57.43,0:36:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,[gate rattles]
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.91,0:37:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,This is where you leave me.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:05.09,0:37:06.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Luther.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.96,0:37:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] What are we gonna do?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:09.44,0:37:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Retire?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.66,0:37:12.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Go fishing?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:14.10,0:37:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.97,0:37:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,This is what I was born to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:20.02,0:37:23.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Luther, I can’t. I can’t.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.46,0:37:25.46,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s nothing you\Nneed to say, brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.11,0:37:27.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.12,0:37:29.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:30.34,0:37:32.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m right where I want to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.25,0:37:33.64,Default,,0,0,0,,[gate rattles]
Dialogue: 0,0:37:34.38,0:37:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan... you need to hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.56,0:37:40.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You go.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.26,0:37:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Find Gabriel.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.05,0:37:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop him.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:46.53,0:37:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,[gate rattles]
Dialogue: 0,0:37:49.01,0:37:50.71,Default,,0,0,0,,For those we never meet.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:55.97,0:37:58.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers]\NFor those we never meet.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.65,0:38:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Gabriel, you son of a bitch,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.91,0:38:28.65,Default,,0,0,0,,no one is safe\Nfrom Phineas Phreak.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:01.12,0:39:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[no audible dialogue]
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.96,0:40:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[Briggs] {\i1}My man Degas.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.05,0:40:06.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Is he dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.58,0:40:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he’s-- he’s alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:11.93,0:40:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Briggs, isn’t it?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.20,0:40:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,But that isn’t your real name.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.16,0:40:20.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.94,0:40:23.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Your real name is Jim Phelps.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:24.73,0:40:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Like your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:28.51,0:40:30.56,Default,,0,0,0,,He was in the service, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.95,0:40:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,He vanished when\Nyou were seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:35.08,0:40:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,You joined to find out\Nwhat happened to him,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:37.17,0:40:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,and you found out\Nhe had legal trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.22,0:40:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,He was offered the choice:
Dialogue: 0,0:40:44.53,0:40:46.45,Default,,0,0,0,,To join the IMF...
Dialogue: 0,0:40:47.49,0:40:49.88,Default,,0,0,0,,or spend the rest of\Nhis life in prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.06,0:40:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like you, Hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.36,0:40:56.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Only in your case, the charge\Nwas murder, I believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:57.11,0:40:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,But let me guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:58.59,0:41:00.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You were framed.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.68,0:41:04.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like your claim\Nyou were framed all those years ago in Prague.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.51,0:41:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How the mission went sideways.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.20,0:41:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,How you lost your whole team.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:11.29,0:41:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Your story had my father\Ndown as a traitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.12,0:41:16.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That’s why you killed him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.52,0:41:24.22,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s true. I wish it weren’t.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.44,0:41:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You think I’m carrying that?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:28.66,0:41:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That I’m here for revenge?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:31.49,0:41:33.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Or... what?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.49,0:41:35.62,Default,,0,0,0,,To clear my father’s name?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:36.84,0:41:38.28,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s my name now.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:39.24,0:41:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.50,0:41:44.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m here
Dialogue: 0,0:41:44.33,0:41:45.94,Default,,0,0,0,,because I know\Nyou’re the reason
Dialogue: 0,0:41:46.11,0:41:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,the world’s staring down\Nthe barrel at Armageddon.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:48.72,0:41:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And I also know\Nit’s not the first time
Dialogue: 0,0:41:50.99,0:41:53.65,Default,,0,0,0,,you’ve gambled with\Nthe fate of the human race.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.47,0:41:57.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And none of that\Nwould matter to me...
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.04,0:42:00.96,Default,,0,0,0,,if you’d ever once
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.13,0:42:02.52,Default,,0,0,0,,been following
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.69,0:42:04.34,Default,,0,0,0,,orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:04.87,0:42:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Briggs.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:06.79,0:42:07.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Phelps.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.00,0:42:10.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Jim.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:11.18,0:42:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The Entity wants you\Nto hate me.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.36,0:42:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s counting on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:16.27,0:42:18.40,Default,,0,0,0,,And the only way to beat it\Nis to do the one thing
Dialogue: 0,0:42:18.58,0:42:21.19,Default,,0,0,0,,it would never expect us to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:22.45,0:42:23.93,Default,,0,0,0,,What’s that?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:33.73,0:42:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,You forget I know you, Hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:36.90,0:42:40.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I know all your IMF mind games.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:40.38,0:42:43.69,Default,,0,0,0,,When this is over,\Nwhen they’re done with you,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.43,0:42:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,you and me,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:46.91,0:42:48.78,Default,,0,0,0,,we’ll have our reckoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.27,0:42:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a shame about your friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:59.49,0:43:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Then again,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.14,0:43:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,you’re used to losing them.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:37.62,0:43:38.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:43.62,0:43:47.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[Kittridge] {\i1}While you’ve been {\i0}\N{\i1}out conducting your own {\i0} {\i1}personal field operation,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.06,0:43:51.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the Entity has infiltrated {\i0}\N{\i1}the nuclear command centers {\i0} {\i1}of India,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:52.11,0:43:55.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Israel, Pakistan,{\i0}\N{\i1}and North Korea.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:56.55,0:43:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Today at 0400 hours Zulu time,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.99,0:44:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,France’s RAMSES\Nfacility was breached.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.90,0:44:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Their entire nuclear arsenal\Nis now under the Entity’s command and control.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:09.86,0:44:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,That leaves only four nations\Nwith secure nuclear arsenals.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:13.96,0:44:18.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}U.K., China, Russia and us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:22.83,0:44:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything you were,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.53,0:44:27.31,Default,,0,0,0,,everything you’ve done
Dialogue: 0,0:44:27.49,0:44:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,has come to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:36.34,0:45:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[thudding]
Dialogue: 0,0:46:08.85,0:46:11.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The CIA Black Vault break-in.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.94,0:46:14.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m sorry, what\Nis a "NOC list"?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:14.95,0:46:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,A complete record of our\Ncovert operatives overseas.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.91,0:46:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,So this is the man who--
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.08,0:46:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Broke into our own Black Vault
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.96,0:46:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and stole the list{\i0}\N{\i1}of our own spies, yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.74,0:46:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He did return the list.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.22,0:46:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s on the next page.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:33.01,0:46:36.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Am I reading this correctly?\NThe Kremlin bombing?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.66,0:46:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,In fairness, the bomb was\Nactually meant to kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.80,0:46:44.80,Default,,0,0,0,,He gassed a security briefing
Dialogue: 0,0:46:44.98,0:46:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}at the National {\i0}\N{\i1}Intelligence Directorate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:47.72,0:46:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,[Sidney] That was\Njust two months ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:52.59,0:46:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You two would have\Nbeen in that meeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.20,0:46:59.68,Default,,0,0,0,,He arrived in the form\Nof Mister Kittridge’s aide.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:59.86,0:47:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And left as Mister Kittridge,\NI believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:04.69,0:47:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[Serling]\NThis explains the handcuffs.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:06.52,0:47:08.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s still not clear\Nwhy he’s here.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:08.61,0:47:12.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Like it or not,\Nwhat we’re looking at is our means of last resort.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:12.18,0:47:15.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Quite possibly our only hope\Nof averting nuclear Armageddon.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:15.79,0:47:19.05,Default,,0,0,0,,If we want to\Ncontrol the Entity,
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.23,0:47:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,we have to deal with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:21.01,0:47:23.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Should he choose to accept.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.19,0:47:24.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[footsteps approaching]
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.33,0:47:37.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Agent Hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:37.25,0:47:39.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President.\NI’m sorry for your loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:46.69,0:47:48.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Please sit.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.53,0:48:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Let’s hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:01.92,0:48:05.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I need that key\Nand the use of a ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.93,0:48:08.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Specifically,\Nan aircraft carrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:08.80,0:48:12.15,Default,,0,0,0,,More specifically,\Nthe {\i1}George H.W. Bush.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:12.32,0:48:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,He wants the "use of"
Dialogue: 0,0:48:14.63,0:48:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,a six-and-a-half billion dollar\Nnuclear-powered military asset.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:19.51,0:48:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,With instructions for\Nthe ship’s commander to accommodate my every request.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:24.08,0:48:25.43,Default,,0,0,0,,To do what exactly?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:25.60,0:48:29.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Use that key and what it opens
Dialogue: 0,0:48:29.56,0:48:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,to kill the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:31.26,0:48:34.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Killing the Entity means\Nthe annihilation of cyberspace.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:34.39,0:48:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,The consequences of which\Nare catastrophic.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:36.91,0:48:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Why the hell would I\Ndo what you suggest?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:39.44,0:48:41.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Respectfully, Madam President,\Nyou have no other choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:41.66,0:48:43.97,Default,,0,0,0,,There is always another choice.\NNo, ma’am.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.14,0:48:46.19,Default,,0,0,0,,In this case, not a good one.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:46.36,0:48:49.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The world’s nuclear powers are\Nin a paranoid downward spiral.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:50.06,0:48:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Every nation had a chance\Nto take their missiles offline,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:53.23,0:48:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,but no one trusted\Nanyone else to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.72,0:49:00.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Your State Department is\Nwarning you that diplomatic channels are breaking down.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:00.29,0:49:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone who still has\Ncontrol of their arsenals is considering a first strike.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.42,0:49:04.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:04.85,0:49:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,The intelligence\Ncommunity knows
Dialogue: 0,0:49:06.29,0:49:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,that the Entity\Nis learning as it goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:07.95,0:49:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s getting smarter,\Nit’s getting stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:10.16,0:49:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,They know that\Nwe have only 72 hours
Dialogue: 0,0:49:12.43,0:49:15.78,Default,,0,0,0,,before every other\Nnuclear arsenal on Earth is under the Entity’s control.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:15.95,0:49:18.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Three days before it focuses\Nthe full force of its energy
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.00,0:49:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,on the toughest,\Nmost secure defense system on the planet: Ours.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.13,0:49:25.52,Default,,0,0,0,,At which point,\Nthe Defense Department will have no choice but to insist
Dialogue: 0,0:49:25.70,0:49:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,that you open that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.40,0:49:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,enter the codes, and launch\Nan all-out preemptive strike
Dialogue: 0,0:49:30.58,0:49:32.36,Default,,0,0,0,,on the world’s eight\Nother nuclear arsenals
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.53,0:49:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,before the Entity\Ntakes control of ours.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:34.41,0:49:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.93,0:49:38.11,Default,,0,0,0,,either you destroy the world\Nor the Entity does.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:38.28,0:49:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,In any case, it is checkmate.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.98,0:49:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[Erika]\NThere is another choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.55,0:49:45.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You could tell me what\Nyou know about that key
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.37,0:49:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,and give us the power\Nto control the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.72,0:49:51.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President, if I believed\Nthat were true, I would tell you everything I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.38,0:49:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.34,0:49:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,You ran the CIA, you know\Npsychological warfare when you see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:56.17,0:49:58.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Just look around.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:58.87,0:50:01.35,Default,,0,0,0,,We are in the Entity’s reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:01.52,0:50:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And I believe it’s\Ncounting on you to stop me.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:04.18,0:50:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,If what you’re saying is true,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.22,0:50:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,how can you be sure the Entity\Ndoesn’t want us to do
Dialogue: 0,0:50:08.35,0:50:10.09,Default,,0,0,0,,exactly what you’re\Nproposing right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:10.27,0:50:11.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] Because it knows\Nyou would never do anything so illogical.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:11.88,0:50:14.10,Default,,0,0,0,,That you would be\Ninsane to trust me.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.27,0:50:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,And that is precisely\Nwhy you should.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:16.01,0:50:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,For once,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:17.88,0:50:19.84,Default,,0,0,0,,let’s let the Entity worry\Nabout what we’re going to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:20.02,0:50:22.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m worried about those three\Nother nations, Madam President,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.93,0:50:24.54,Default,,0,0,0,,still in control\Nof their arsenals.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:24.72,0:50:28.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Nations who could panic\Nand launch a full-scale attack
Dialogue: 0,0:50:28.46,0:50:32.12,Default,,0,0,0,,while he’s out there\Nwith an aircraft carrier, doing God knows what!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:32.29,0:50:34.94,Default,,0,0,0,,While he’s out there\Ntrying to kill the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.12,0:50:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Which we all know\Nis a terrible idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.56,0:50:40.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President, please. I’m\Nasking for three days while you
Dialogue: 0,0:50:40.86,0:50:42.69,Default,,0,0,0,,keep the world calm.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:42.87,0:50:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.17,0:50:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Have I ever...
Dialogue: 0,0:50:45.91,0:50:47.35,Default,,0,0,0,,let you down before?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:47.52,0:50:49.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And when the Entity decides\Nto attack before then?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:49.70,0:50:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,It has enough missiles\Nto kill billions already. Why hasn’t it done it?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:52.35,0:50:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Because it’s a machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:54.27,0:50:56.40,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s thinking like a machine.\NNo, its thinking...
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.58,0:50:57.93,Default,,0,0,0,,[NSA representative]\NIts thinking is binary.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:58.10,0:50:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,...is dictated by what\Nit’s learned from us.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:00.10,0:51:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It hasn’t launched because\Nit doesn’t have total control.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.58,0:51:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It needs the world’s entire\Natomic arsenal to guarantee the desired outcome:
Dialogue: 0,0:51:07.24,0:51:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,The total annihilation\Nof humankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.20,0:51:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.81,0:51:13.90,Default,,0,0,0,,it is going to wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:14.07,0:51:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,[alarm beeping]
Dialogue: 0,0:51:35.48,0:51:39.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[Erika] Northwood Nuclear\NOperations and Targeting Centre in London has been breached.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.14,0:51:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,The United Kingdom has\Nlost control of its arsenal.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.02,0:51:50.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I will ask you one last time.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.41,0:51:51.80,Default,,0,0,0,,What does this unlock?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.98,0:51:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Erika,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:53.20,0:51:55.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I need you to trust me
Dialogue: 0,0:51:56.16,0:51:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,one last time.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.24,0:51:59.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me when I tell you:
Dialogue: 0,0:51:59.90,0:52:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,When that clock\Nruns out in 72 hours,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:03.77,0:52:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I will press that button,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:05.60,0:52:08.69,Default,,0,0,0,,and that will be\Nyour responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:08.86,0:52:10.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President--
Dialogue: 0,0:52:10.61,0:52:11.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Sergeants,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.91,0:52:13.61,Default,,0,0,0,,lock him up!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:18.00,0:52:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,[helicopter whirring]
Dialogue: 0,0:52:34.54,0:52:36.76,Default,,0,0,0,,[soldier]\NYou heard the President.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:39.81,0:52:42.16,Default,,0,0,0,,You have 72 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.51,0:52:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,She says you’ll know what to do\Nwith this when the time comes.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:56.35,0:52:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.04,0:52:59.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.02,0:53:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I left you a message on there\Nfor when this is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:24.38,0:53:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan]\NYou can tell me yourself...
Dialogue: 0,0:53:27.38,0:53:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,after.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:30.47,0:53:34.17,Default,,0,0,0,,They made us take an oath\Nwhen they gave us the choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.69,0:53:38.43,Default,,0,0,0,,We live and die in the shadows
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.13,0:53:41.18,Default,,0,0,0,,for those we hold close...
Dialogue: 0,0:53:42.44,0:53:44.05,Default,,0,0,0,,and for those we never meet.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:44.22,0:53:46.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I know what’s on your mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:47.88,0:53:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You did the right thing\Nwhen you kept the key.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:52.58,0:53:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,You’ve always been\Non the right side, brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:55.71,0:53:57.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Always.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:58.10,0:53:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Never forget,
Dialogue: 0,0:54:00.15,0:54:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,our lives are not defined\Nby any one action.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:05.55,0:54:06.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Our lives
Dialogue: 0,0:54:06.81,0:54:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,are the sum of our choices.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:10.42,0:54:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no regrets.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:13.47,0:54:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither should you.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:53.59,0:54:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[jet engines screaming]
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.60,0:55:06.69,Default,,0,0,0,,[indistinct chatter]
Dialogue: 0,0:55:11.79,0:55:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,[indistinct chatter]
Dialogue: 0,0:55:18.49,0:55:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[chatter continues faintly]
Dialogue: 0,0:55:43.12,0:55:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[Neely] Did Erika--
Dialogue: 0,0:55:44.43,0:55:45.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Did the President
Dialogue: 0,0:55:45.73,0:55:47.65,Default,,0,0,0,,tell you the meaning\Nbehind this note?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.26,0:55:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,No, ma’am.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:49.96,0:55:54.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Serbia. May 22nd, 1996.\NWe both lost someone we loved.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:54.18,0:55:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:55.96,0:55:58.83,Default,,0,0,0,,All because no one in\Nauthority would take a risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:01.05,0:56:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m sitting on\Na powder keg, mister.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:03.53,0:56:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Just over that horizon is\NRussia’s only aircraft carrier, the {\i1}Admiral Kuznetsov.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:09.19,0:56:11.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I am one wrong move away\Nfrom the first shoot-out
Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.46,0:56:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,between two flattops\Nsince World War II.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:14.76,0:56:18.42,Default,,0,0,0,,One flinch from\Ntouching off World War III.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.03,0:56:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,And you’re asking me\Nto fly you directly into the eye of the storm.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:23.51,0:56:25.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, ma’am, I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:26.73,0:56:28.95,Default,,0,0,0,,What exactly are\Nyou looking for?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:29.60,0:56:30.91,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}SOSUS.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.08,0:56:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Short for "Sound{\i0}\N{\i1}Surveillance System."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:33.48,0:56:35.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a worldwide network\Nof undersea acoustic cables
Dialogue: 0,0:56:35.61,0:56:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,dating back to the Cold War.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.70,0:56:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,If an undersea event\Nof any significance happens anywhere in the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:40.27,0:56:44.23,Default,,0,0,0,,one of these listening stations\Nwill pinpoint that event to the square meter.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:44.40,0:56:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] {\i1}And one of{\i0}\N{\i1}these SOSUS stations{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:46.05,0:56:47.88,Default,,0,0,0,,will have recorded\Nour missing Russian submarine’s
Dialogue: 0,0:56:48.06,0:56:50.41,Default,,0,0,0,,impact on the sea floor\Nin the winter of 2012.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:50.58,0:56:53.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Without ever understanding\Nthe significance of the event.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:53.93,0:56:56.28,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Whereas\Nthe Russians know when the {\i1}Sevastopol{\i0}vanished.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:56.46,0:56:58.24,Default,,0,0,0,,They’re just not\Nexactly sure where.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:58.42,0:56:59.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[In French]\NWe must make a choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:00.07,0:57:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji speaking French]
Dialogue: 0,0:57:01.72,0:57:03.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Which one
Dialogue: 0,0:57:03.33,0:57:07.12,Default,,0,0,0,,out of all these SOSUS stations\Npicked up the event?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:07.29,0:57:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,We know the bodies\Nof the {\i1}Sevastopol’s{\i0}crew were recovered in sea ice.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:10.30,0:57:12.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And since they were recovered {\i0}\N{\i1}by Inuit fishermen...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:13.08,0:57:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re guessing it went down\Nsomewhere in the Arctic.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:15.30,0:57:18.65,Default,,0,0,0,,A search area of roughly\Nfive and a half million square miles.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:18.83,0:57:22.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Meaning the most likely SOSUS\Nstation to pick it up is...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:22.31,0:57:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,This one. In the Bering Sea.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:25.09,0:57:26.48,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] St. Matthew Island.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:27.62,0:57:29.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The Russians will know this.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:29.75,0:57:31.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Why haven’t they just\Nstormed the island already?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.67,0:57:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Because St. Matthew is\Na U.S. Government installation.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.15,0:57:37.20,Default,,0,0,0,,An overt act of aggression\Nwould trigger World War III.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:37.37,0:57:39.68,Default,,0,0,0,,But now Armageddon is coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:39.85,0:57:42.11,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] And the Russians\Nhave nothing to lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:42.28,0:57:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Do your friends know they’re\Nwalking into a potential siege?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:46.03,0:57:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,They know that’s the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:48.16,0:57:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,So, to retrieve the Entity’s\Nsource code from {\i1}Sevastopol,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:51.38,0:57:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan needs\Nthe precise coordinates from St. Matthew Island.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:54.43,0:57:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And a submarine, obviously.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:56.69,0:57:59.08,Default,,0,0,0,,One that’s willing to take you\Nwhere you want to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:59.26,0:58:00.61,Default,,0,0,0,,No questions asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:00.78,0:58:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma’am.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:02.17,0:58:03.48,Default,,0,0,0,,And that’s assuming
Dialogue: 0,0:58:03.65,0:58:05.65,Default,,0,0,0,,your friends can actually\Nget the coordinates.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:05.83,0:58:10.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Which we’re expected\Nto transmit for fifteen minutes every two hours...
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.49,0:58:14.93,Default,,0,0,0,,In the hope that\NEthan is somehow able to receive our signal.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:15.10,0:58:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you intend to make it\Nout from under the ice cap?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:17.93,0:58:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,After sending me\Nthe coordinates, my team will make their way there.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:21.72,0:58:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Now, Ethan will\Nhave a VHF transmitter
Dialogue: 0,0:58:23.89,0:58:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,which will enable us to\Nzero in on his exact location under the ice.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:27.24,0:58:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}All we have to do then{\i0}\N{\i1}is grab a chainsaw and--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:29.94,0:58:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What? Cut a hole in the ice cap\Nand just pull Ethan out?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:33.68,0:58:36.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang on. Depending on\Nhow deep that wreck is,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:36.30,0:58:39.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan will have severe\Ndecompression sickness before he reaches the surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:39.78,0:58:42.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Which is why we have this.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:43.61,0:58:45.53,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] What the hell is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:45.70,0:58:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a state-of-the-art\Ninflatable hyperbaric decompression chamber.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:50.66,0:58:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re not serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:54.88,0:58:57.75,Default,,0,0,0,,What?\NYou mean to tell me that Ethan’s life
Dialogue: 0,0:58:57.93,0:59:00.02,Default,,0,0,0,,and the fate of\Nall life on Earth
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.19,0:59:04.41,Default,,0,0,0,,depends on us all meeting\Nat the exact same place
Dialogue: 0,0:59:04.58,0:59:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,at the exact same time,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:07.07,0:59:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,somewhere in\Nthe frozen Bering Sea...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.24,0:59:12.15,Default,,0,0,0,,with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:12.33,0:59:13.59,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:13.77,0:59:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And what if he drowns\Nbefore we get there?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:15.99,0:59:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,In all likelihood, he will.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:18.25,0:59:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,But in water that cold,\Nthe hypothermia will slow down his metabolic functions
Dialogue: 0,0:59:22.56,0:59:24.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and buy us time to revive him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:26.08,0:59:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s your plan?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:28.96,0:59:29.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:30.04,0:59:32.57,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s our plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:36.05,0:59:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The only submarine\Nin range is the {\i1}Ohio.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.49,0:59:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Jack Bledsoe’s boat.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:41.36,0:59:43.49,Default,,0,0,0,,When submerged,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:43.67,0:59:46.89,Default,,0,0,0,,he’s reachable only\Nby VLF radio-- shielded from any digital transmission.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:47.06,0:59:50.06,Default,,0,0,0,,That means he is\Nimmune to this thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:50.24,0:59:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,But only if he stays submerged.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:52.68,0:59:55.64,Default,,0,0,0,,An Osprey can get you there\Nin two hours, but it won’t have enough fuel to wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:55.81,0:59:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s no other choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:57.51,1:00:00.56,Default,,0,0,0,,If Bledsoe receives my command,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:00.73,1:00:03.21,Default,,0,0,0,,if he believes it\Nto be authentic,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:03.38,1:00:05.95,Default,,0,0,0,,he might come to\Nperiscope depth.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:06.12,1:00:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,He might wait thirty seconds.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:08.61,1:00:11.87,Default,,0,0,0,,If you are even\None minute late...
Dialogue: 0,1:00:12.04,1:00:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Just give me this chance.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:49.69,1:00:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[NRO representative]\N{\i1}You let Hunt go?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:51.82,1:00:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s what I said.\NWith the key?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:54.87,1:00:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He couldn’t do much without it.\NSo where is he now?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:57.57,1:00:59.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Somewhere in the\NNorthern Pacific, I assume.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:59.87,1:01:03.48,Default,,0,0,0,,You gave him an\Naircraft carrier?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:03.66,1:01:07.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I am the Commander in Chief\Nof the Armed Forces, Mister Secretary.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:07.32,1:01:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,It is my aircraft carrier
Dialogue: 0,1:01:09.67,1:01:11.02,Default,,0,0,0,,and I do with it as I please.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:11.19,1:01:13.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You knew this would happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:13.28,1:01:14.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I suspected.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.54,1:01:15.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You could have\Nat least told us.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:16.02,1:01:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I just did.\NAnd now you’re excused.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:18.37,1:01:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President--\NThat will be all.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:23.42,1:01:25.12,Default,,0,0,0,,[scoffs]
Dialogue: 0,1:01:37.00,1:01:38.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn’t tell you.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:38.48,1:01:42.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It had to be my responsibility\Nand mine alone.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:42.18,1:01:44.31,Default,,0,0,0,,And I had to buy Hunt time.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:44.48,1:01:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone could have\Ntried to stop him.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:46.62,1:01:49.01,Default,,0,0,0,,They may not agree with you,\Nbut they do respect your authority.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:49.18,1:01:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Before this is over,\Nsomeone will panic.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:52.80,1:01:55.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone will try to stop me.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:04.02,1:02:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Another field trip.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:07.20,1:02:09.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You know where he’s at?\NI know where he’s gonna end up.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:10.55,1:02:12.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Let’s surprise him.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:34.27,1:02:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Now remember,\Ngovernments would kill
Dialogue: 0,1:02:36.14,1:02:38.10,Default,,0,0,0,,to know what we know\Nabout the {\i1}Sevastopol.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:38.28,1:02:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a CIA station
Dialogue: 0,1:02:40.54,1:02:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,run by seasoned field agents\Ntrained to get information and never, ever give it.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:45.20,1:02:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell them nothing\Nabout our real mission. Just let me do the talking.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:54.64,1:02:56.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:03:05.30,1:03:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,[person speaks Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:03:07.83,1:03:09.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:03:12.96,1:03:14.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:15.66,1:03:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Can I help you?\NI certainly hope so. Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:18.19,1:03:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re looking for the SOSUS\Nlistening station.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:20.84,1:03:23.93,Default,,0,0,0,,You found it, friend. I’m\Nthe station chief, Bill Donloe.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:24.10,1:03:25.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My wife, Tapeesa.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:26.93,1:03:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Hello. How do you do?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:29.46,1:03:31.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, nice to meet you, Bill.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:31.50,1:03:32.76,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re researchers from\Nthe British Seismological--
Dialogue: 0,1:03:32.94,1:03:34.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m sorry, did you say Donloe?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:34.81,1:03:36.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s right.\N[Benji] Bill.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:36.20,1:03:38.03,Default,,0,0,0,,William Donloe?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:38.21,1:03:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Langley Donloe?\NBlack Vault Donloe?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:40.77,1:03:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The same.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:42.25,1:03:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And you are?\N[chuckles]
Dialogue: 0,1:03:43.60,1:03:46.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t believe...\NAre you ser...
Dialogue: 0,1:03:46.21,1:03:48.65,Default,,0,0,0,,This guy is a coding legend.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:48.83,1:03:51.40,Default,,0,0,0,,He designed the CIA mainframe\Nat Langley. The Black Vault.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:51.57,1:03:54.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s the most secure database\Non the planet. It’s completely impenetrable.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:54.48,1:03:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, if it were impenetrable,\NI wouldn’t be here.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:57.79,1:04:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,The Vault was breached in ’96
Dialogue: 0,1:04:00.31,1:04:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,and the agency shipped me\Nout the same day.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:02.53,1:04:04.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Been here ever since.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:04.36,1:04:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait. So you mean to say you’ve\Nbeen on this island for...
Dialogue: 0,1:04:09.80,1:04:11.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Thirty years.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.07,1:04:15.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Just out of curiosity, how do\Nyou know about the Black Vault?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:16.90,1:04:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s highly classified.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:19.86,1:04:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers] Tick-tock,\Ntick-tock, tick-tock.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:21.42,1:04:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry. Who did\Nyou say you were?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:23.69,1:04:25.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Just tell the man\Nwhy we’re here.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:25.64,1:04:26.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Donloe. Bill.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:26.95,1:04:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if we could\Ntell you the truth,
Dialogue: 0,1:04:28.52,1:04:30.04,Default,,0,0,0,,you wouldn’t believe it.\NI wouldn’t.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:30.21,1:04:31.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The heart of the matter\Nis that we need access
Dialogue: 0,1:04:31.96,1:04:34.57,Default,,0,0,0,,to all your SOSUS data\Nfrom late winter 2012.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:34.74,1:04:37.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise the world will\Ncease to exist in a few days.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:39.35,1:04:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s happening, isn’t it?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:42.49,1:04:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,The Entity.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.40,1:04:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ve tried to warn people\Nabout it for years, but...
Dialogue: 0,1:04:49.23,1:04:50.84,Default,,0,0,0,,no one would listen.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:51.76,1:04:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you help us?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:53.93,1:04:55.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish I could.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:56.37,1:04:58.20,Default,,0,0,0,,[footsteps approaching]
Dialogue: 0,1:05:04.25,1:05:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,[dishes clattering]\N[door slams]
Dialogue: 0,1:05:13.78,1:05:16.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[Russian soldier]\NPlease come in.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:16.39,1:05:19.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Make yourself comfortable.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:23.09,1:05:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[airman 1] Sir! Wake up!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:25.14,1:05:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Wake up, sir!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:26.92,1:05:29.57,Default,,0,0,0,,We got problems. Real problems.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:29.75,1:05:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What’s happening?\NIt’s the {\i1}Admiral Kuznetsov.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:34.41,1:05:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,[airman 1]\NWe got to get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:36.32,1:05:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re in Ivan’s\Nthreat zone, man.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:38.72,1:05:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Any sign of the {\i1}Ohio?{\i0}\NNo, sir. And we’re at bingo.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:41.55,1:05:44.21,Default,,0,0,0,,If I don’t turn around soon,\Nwe won’t have enough fuel to get us back to the boat.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:44.38,1:05:46.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Anything on the radio?\NNothing but static on VHF.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:46.86,1:05:49.12,Default,,0,0,0,,If your friends are\Nbroadcasting a signal, we can’t hear it.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:49.29,1:05:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Just take us into a hover.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:50.56,1:05:52.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, we are at bingo.\NFive minutes!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:52.51,1:05:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Just give me five\Nminutes. Please!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:58.04,1:05:59.52,Default,,0,0,0,,We can give you one.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:59.69,1:06:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Decel.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:07.22,1:06:09.44,Default,,0,0,0,,What are we doing in a hover?\NWe got to bug out!
Dialogue: 0,1:06:09.62,1:06:10.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Bogies at two.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:13.23,1:06:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,They’re showing us\Ntheir missiles, man.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:17.36,1:06:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s the only warning\Nwe’re gonna get.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:19.41,1:06:22.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Russian Aircraft...\NThis is some World War III shit here. We got to go!
Dialogue: 0,1:06:22.72,1:06:24.29,Default,,0,0,0,,[airman 2] International\Nairspace. No challenge.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:24.46,1:06:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I repeat:\NNo challenge is intended.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:29.81,1:06:31.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Where the hell are you going?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:36.51,1:06:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,1:06:43.39,1:06:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,[shuddering]
Dialogue: 0,1:06:58.41,1:07:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[shudders]
Dialogue: 0,1:07:02.84,1:07:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping]
Dialogue: 0,1:07:10.72,1:07:11.98,Default,,0,0,0,,[electricity crackling]
Dialogue: 0,1:07:33.35,1:07:36.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you, Ethan?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:44.63,1:07:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,[shivering, coughing]
Dialogue: 0,1:07:55.90,1:07:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,[shivers]
Dialogue: 0,1:08:16.40,1:08:18.40,Default,,0,0,0,,You must be Captain Bledsoe.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:18.57,1:08:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And you must be\Nout of your mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:23.23,1:08:26.06,Default,,0,0,0,,What exactly was the plan\Nif we hadn’t shown up?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:26.23,1:08:29.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, I really hadn’t\Nthought that far ahead.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:29.24,1:08:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:31.76,1:08:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Nope.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:37.98,1:08:40.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] Rear Admiral Neely\Nsends her regards.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:40.42,1:08:43.60,Default,,0,0,0,,She told me to\Nexpect a green flare.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:45.34,1:08:46.78,Default,,0,0,0,,She never mentioned a Taser.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:46.95,1:08:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Mind telling me\Nwhat this is all about?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:49.17,1:08:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,My mission is classified.\NUh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:51.43,1:08:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I need you to take me north.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:53.17,1:08:54.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Continue.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:54.78,1:08:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m expecting a set\Nof exact coordinates
Dialogue: 0,1:08:56.35,1:08:58.05,Default,,0,0,0,,via Morse code transmission.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:58.22,1:09:01.35,Default,,0,0,0,,And just how exactly\Ndo you expect to receive them down here?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:01.53,1:09:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You’d have to come\Nto periscope depth.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:04.40,1:09:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Raise the antenna.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:06.14,1:09:08.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Signal-scan the low\Nend of the VHF band.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:08.36,1:09:11.06,Default,,0,0,0,,For how long?\NFifteen minutes.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:11.23,1:09:15.15,Default,,0,0,0,,That would give the Russians\Nfifteen minutes to pinpoint our location.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:15.33,1:09:19.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Starting at noon,\Nand every two hours after that,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:19.33,1:09:23.16,Default,,0,0,0,,until my team sends\Nme those coordinates.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:26.73,1:09:28.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[Bledsoe] North is\Nthe Bering Sea, mister.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:28.73,1:09:32.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now every submarine\Nin the Russian Pacific Fleet is up there.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:32.30,1:09:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,My primary mission is to\Nlock down their positions
Dialogue: 0,1:09:34.74,1:09:36.48,Default,,0,0,0,,and ascertain\Nwhat they’re up to.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:36.65,1:09:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m thinking you\Nknow the answer.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.00,1:09:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] What is that?\NThat’s St. Matthew Island.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:43.35,1:09:45.66,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s nothing there but an\Nold SOSUS listening station.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:45.83,1:09:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no, that right next to it.\NWhat is that?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:52.41,1:09:53.85,Default,,0,0,0,,[Bledsoe] That’s the {\i1}Losharik.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:09:54.02,1:09:56.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what that is?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:57.06,1:09:59.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a mini-sub,\NRussian Special Forces.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:59.54,1:10:01.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Get yourself\Na gold star, mister.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:01.59,1:10:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Aerial recon spotted it\Noff St. Matthew Island just over an hour ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:05.59,1:10:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s deployed from this:
Dialogue: 0,1:10:07.94,1:10:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The {\i1}Belgorod.{\i0}The deadliest\Nsubmarine in the Russian Navy.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:11.56,1:10:15.52,Default,,0,0,0,,My secondary mission is\Nto locate that bastard and hold it at risk.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:15.69,1:10:18.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The {\i1}Losharik{\i0}means\Nit’s somewhere close by.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:20.74,1:10:22.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You have people on that island.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:22.44,1:10:25.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s where your coordinates\Nare coming from.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:27.92,1:10:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you help me?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:29.83,1:10:31.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Mister...
Dialogue: 0,1:10:33.40,1:10:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,if you want to poke the bear,
Dialogue: 0,1:10:36.71,1:10:39.32,Default,,0,0,0,,oh, you’ve come\Nto the right man.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:41.28,1:10:42.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Like to speak with\Nyour divemaster, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:42.72,1:10:44.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:44.94,1:10:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:46.55,1:10:48.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Have Pills meet our guest\Nin the FORECON quarters.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:49.03,1:10:50.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[chief] Aye, sir.\NThis way, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:53.25,1:10:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[Donloe] As I’ve explained\Nto our friends here,
Dialogue: 0,1:10:55.08,1:10:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t have\Nthe data they want.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:57.21,1:11:01.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The agency ignored my request\Nto upgrade our system for a decade.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:01.30,1:11:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,One day a team shows up,\Nunannounced,
Dialogue: 0,1:11:03.96,1:11:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and refits the entire system {\i0}\N{\i1}in a matter of days.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:06.74,1:11:08.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m guessing this is\Nthe winter of 2012.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:08.61,1:11:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Right. The old system\Nran on magnetic tapes,
Dialogue: 0,1:11:11.22,1:11:12.92,Default,,0,0,0,,backed up to 8-inch floppies.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:13.09,1:11:14.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}These were in the{\i0}\N{\i1}dog shed out back.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:14.62,1:11:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,These boxes might\Ncontain the coordinates
Dialogue: 0,1:11:17.40,1:11:18.97,Default,,0,0,0,,you’re all looking for,
Dialogue: 0,1:11:19.14,1:11:21.40,Default,,0,0,0,,but I don’t have a reader.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:21.58,1:11:24.10,Default,,0,0,0,,That was also\Ntaken away in 2012.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:24.28,1:11:26.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You expect him to build one.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:26.46,1:11:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I came for coordinates,\Nnot boxes.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:29.63,1:11:31.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Supposing you find\Nthe coordinates. What happens to my team?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:32.07,1:11:35.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I will take the coordinates to\Nmy superiors. My men wait here.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:35.64,1:11:37.34,Default,,0,0,0,,When we have located\Nwhat we’re looking for,
Dialogue: 0,1:11:37.51,1:11:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,my men will leave\Nand you will not be harmed.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:40.56,1:11:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you believe\Nthat if you were me?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:42.73,1:11:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I would not.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:45.00,1:11:47.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You have one hour\Nto build the drive.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:49.48,1:11:50.57,Default,,0,0,0,,What’s your name?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:50.74,1:11:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Koltsov.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:51.83,1:11:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Your first name?\NCaptain.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:54.66,1:11:57.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Koltsov, I’m Grace.\NThat’s Benji.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:57.57,1:11:59.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Could we just, for five\Nminutes, be human beings?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:00.05,1:12:03.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Not Russians, not Americans,\Njust people that want to see our loved ones again.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:03.71,1:12:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no one. Not even a dog.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:07.06,1:12:10.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you certainly\Ndon’t have this key.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:10.33,1:12:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,The cruciform key\Nthat grants the holder access to the Podkova.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:13.98,1:12:15.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if you have\Nthe coordinates,
Dialogue: 0,1:12:15.90,1:12:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,you still can’t safely retrieve\Nthe Entity’s source code
Dialogue: 0,1:12:18.07,1:12:19.81,Default,,0,0,0,,without our help.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:20.90,1:12:22.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You have another key,
Dialogue: 0,1:12:23.69,1:12:25.08,Default,,0,0,0,,don’t you?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:26.47,1:12:27.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You’ve had one all along.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:28.08,1:12:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What you don’t have\Nare the coordinates.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:31.74,1:12:34.18,Default,,0,0,0,,And when you build the drive,
Dialogue: 0,1:12:34.35,1:12:36.31,Default,,0,0,0,,we will have that.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:36.48,1:12:39.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, let’s try something else.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:39.36,1:12:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,What if I told you\Nthat we have a friend
Dialogue: 0,1:12:41.79,1:12:46.10,Default,,0,0,0,,who’s been disavowed by\Nhis own government because he refused to hand over this key?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:46.27,1:12:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Our friend is out there\Nright now, independent from any chain of command,
Dialogue: 0,1:12:49.63,1:12:51.20,Default,,0,0,0,,waiting for us\Nto transmit those coordinates.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:51.37,1:12:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,And he will stop at nothing
Dialogue: 0,1:12:53.37,1:12:56.76,Default,,0,0,0,,to safely retrieve the Podkova\Nand use the source code stored on it
Dialogue: 0,1:12:56.94,1:12:58.38,Default,,0,0,0,,to destroy the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:58.55,1:13:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And not for the sake of\Nany one nation, but for all.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:00.59,1:13:04.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t you see?\NThe Entity is counting on us to distrust each other.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:04.47,1:13:05.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Please...
Dialogue: 0,1:13:05.86,1:13:07.95,Default,,0,0,0,,let us complete our mission.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:08.12,1:13:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,We are not enemies.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:10.78,1:13:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you believe\Nthat if you were me?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:14.39,1:13:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales]
Dialogue: 0,1:13:17.44,1:13:18.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[softly] No.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:19.96,1:13:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I suppose I wouldn’t.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:21.88,1:13:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You have one hour.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:28.45,1:13:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the Mark\NVII pressure suit,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:31.19,1:13:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,specifically designed\Nto reduce decompression time
Dialogue: 0,1:13:33.63,1:13:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,after diving profound depths.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:35.67,1:13:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,It does this by means\Nof an exotic mixture of oxygen and inert gases.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:39.81,1:13:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You’ll need to do\Nan extended breathe-up for your body to handle it.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:42.55,1:13:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly what kind of gases\Nare we talking about?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:44.81,1:13:46.51,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s classified.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:46.68,1:13:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[Pills] Assuming you’re on task\Nfor twenty minutes or less,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:49.21,1:13:53.82,Default,,0,0,0,,your time in decompression will\Nbe cut down from days to hours.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:54.95,1:13:56.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Theoretically.\NTheoretically?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:57.08,1:14:00.69,Default,,0,0,0,,We haven’t tested the Mark VII\Nbelow 300 feet.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:00.87,1:14:03.61,Default,,0,0,0,,[diver 1] To conserve air,\Nyou’ll need to make a fast descent.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:03.79,1:14:06.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means guaranteed HPNS.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:06.75,1:14:09.41,Default,,0,0,0,,High Pressure Nervous Syndrome.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:09.58,1:14:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You should expect tremors,
Dialogue: 0,1:14:11.40,1:14:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,shakes, dizziness,
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.19,1:14:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,disorientation,\Nand mental confusion.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:16.76,1:14:20.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And all of it\Nunder extreme pressure.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:20.72,1:14:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[Pills] Even if the Mark\NVII works as designed,
Dialogue: 0,1:14:23.98,1:14:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you still won’t have enough {\i0}\N{\i1}mixture for a slow ascent.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:14:27.16,1:14:29.68,Default,,0,0,0,,That means you’re guaranteed\Nto get the bends.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:31.29,1:14:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,[Pills] Nitrogen\Nin your muscle tissue expands into your bloodstream.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:35.43,1:14:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,[diver 2] Excruciating pain.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:37.78,1:14:39.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Convulsions.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:40.56,1:14:43.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Complete loss of\Nmuscle control.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:43.26,1:14:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You’ll have maybe\Ntwenty minutes to get to the decompression chamber.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:48.61,1:14:51.31,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]\N[divers shouting]
Dialogue: 0,1:14:51.49,1:14:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,And without the\Ndecompression chamber...
Dialogue: 0,1:14:53.79,1:14:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,[Pills] You’re a dead man.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:58.45,1:15:01.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[Bledsoe] Another VHF scan\Ncame and went.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:01.41,1:15:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,If your friends\Nare broadcasting,
Dialogue: 0,1:15:03.63,1:15:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,we still haven’t picked it up.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:19.30,1:15:21.08,Default,,0,0,0,,[whirring]
Dialogue: 0,1:15:21.26,1:15:23.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, come on,\Ncome on, come on, come on.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:23.69,1:15:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,1:15:24.82,1:15:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,[dogs barking in the distance]
Dialogue: 0,1:15:30.40,1:15:33.80,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s the sled dogs\Nout in the barn. It’s coming up to dinnertime.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:37.53,1:15:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,[dogs continue barking]
Dialogue: 0,1:15:46.45,1:15:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m gonna let you in\Non a little secret, friend.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:48.41,1:15:51.76,Default,,0,0,0,,There are no coordinates\Non any of these disks.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:51.94,1:15:55.60,Default,,0,0,0,,That "refit"\Nfourteen years ago?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:55.77,1:15:58.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It had all the stench\Nof a cover-up.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:00.47,1:16:03.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the top man{\i0}\N{\i1}talked down to Tapeesa.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:16:04.39,1:16:06.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not like that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:16:06.78,1:16:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I never told them\Nabout these backups.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:09.48,1:16:12.35,Default,,0,0,0,,And when they left,\NI went through every one of them myself.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:12.52,1:16:14.74,Default,,0,0,0,,A lone event stood out.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:14.92,1:16:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling]
Dialogue: 0,1:16:16.27,1:16:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A massive undersea implosion{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:16:18.62,1:16:20.97,Default,,0,0,0,,about a month\Nbefore they arrived to take everything away.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:21.14,1:16:24.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Naturally, I didn’t\Nunderstand the significance.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:24.58,1:16:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,But I noted the coordinates\Nand then
Dialogue: 0,1:16:27.71,1:16:29.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I destroyed the only disk.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:32.02,1:16:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,[quietly] Are you saying you\Nknow where the {\i1}Sevastopol{\i0}is?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:36.90,1:16:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Down to the square meter.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:42.34,1:16:45.04,Default,,0,0,0,,[dogs continue barking]
Dialogue: 0,1:16:51.17,1:16:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Dinnertime.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:55.48,1:16:57.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Can my wife please\Ntend to the dogs?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:57.96,1:17:00.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t concentrate\Nwith this racket.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:15.07,1:17:17.64,Default,,0,0,0,,[in Inuktitut] The coordinates.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:17.81,1:17:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Be careful.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:24.38,1:17:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I love you.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:26.86,1:17:29.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers in Inuktitut]\NI will see you again.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:30.47,1:17:32.39,Default,,0,0,0,,She’s gonna need some help.I’ll go!
Dialogue: 0,1:17:34.65,1:17:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I could use the air.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:38.39,1:17:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,[in Russian] Go with them.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:46.49,1:17:47.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[door opens]
Dialogue: 0,1:17:48.79,1:17:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,[door closes]
Dialogue: 0,1:18:02.16,1:18:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,[breathing heavily]
Dialogue: 0,1:18:05.64,1:18:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[Bledsoe] Five minutes\Nto the next broadcast window.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:08.21,1:18:11.30,Default,,0,0,0,,We’ll be under the ice cap\Nsoon and lose all comms.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:12.56,1:18:15.48,Default,,0,0,0,,This will be our last chance.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:25.74,1:18:32.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[dogs barking, howling]
Dialogue: 0,1:18:48.42,1:18:50.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[clattering]
Dialogue: 0,1:18:53.55,1:18:55.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[dogs continue barking]
Dialogue: 0,1:18:58.04,1:19:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,[breathing heavily]
Dialogue: 0,1:19:13.27,1:19:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief of the Watch,\Nraise number one comms antenna.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:30.42,1:19:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:19:31.72,1:19:33.64,Default,,0,0,0,,What? Wait! Wait, Hagar.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:33.81,1:19:34.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:36.47,1:19:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait. What is this?\NWhat is this?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:39.25,1:19:41.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You won’t stop\Nthe Entity, Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:42.95,1:19:44.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t let you.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:44.82,1:19:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,[both grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:19:49.57,1:19:51.18,Default,,0,0,0,,[dogs barking]
Dialogue: 0,1:19:52.09,1:19:54.18,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:19:54.35,1:19:56.40,Default,,0,0,0,,[dog wails]
Dialogue: 0,1:19:56.57,1:19:57.53,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:19:59.75,1:20:01.06,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]\N[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:04.67,1:20:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:06.71,1:20:08.41,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:10.46,1:20:11.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:12.76,1:20:14.63,Default,,0,0,0,,[all grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:16.86,1:20:17.86,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:28.39,1:20:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Donloe, get to the radio!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:30.30,1:20:31.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Send the coordinates!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:34.44,1:20:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:38.44,1:20:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:44.54,1:20:45.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:46.80,1:20:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,[hisses]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:49.37,1:20:51.15,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:55.15,1:20:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouting]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:00.33,1:21:01.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:03.68,1:21:05.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[radio officer] Conn radio!\NVHF Morse code incoming.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:05.99,1:21:07.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Radio, on speaker.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:09.87,1:21:11.74,Default,,0,0,0,,[clicking]\N[people grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:11.91,1:21:13.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:27.67,1:21:29.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]\N[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:32.02,1:21:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouting in pain]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:34.50,1:21:35.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Hagar,
Dialogue: 0,1:21:35.72,1:21:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,you’ve spent too much...
Dialogue: 0,1:21:38.68,1:21:39.86,Default,,0,0,0,,time
Dialogue: 0,1:21:40.03,1:21:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,on the Internet!
Dialogue: 0,1:21:41.72,1:21:43.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouting]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:47.51,1:21:49.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouting]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:50.08,1:21:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,[both grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:55.78,1:21:57.52,Default,,0,0,0,,[Hagar straining]
Dialogue: 0,1:21:59.13,1:22:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouting]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:02.53,1:22:03.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:04.40,1:22:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:11.75,1:22:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[all grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:18.32,1:22:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[struggling]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:19.41,1:22:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:29.60,1:22:30.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[clicking]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:31.12,1:22:32.60,Default,,0,0,0,,[in Russian] He’s\Nsending the coordinates.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:32.77,1:22:34.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Our people are listening.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:34.99,1:22:37.51,Default,,0,0,0,,The roof is collapsing.\NGet out.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:39.74,1:22:40.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[coughing]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:40.83,1:22:42.31,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting][shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:42.48,1:22:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:48.57,1:22:49.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:22:54.19,1:22:55.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[gagging]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:05.81,1:23:07.94,Default,,0,0,0,,[coughs]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:08.11,1:23:11.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:14.64,1:23:16.64,Default,,0,0,0,,[Hagar shouting]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:19.86,1:23:21.12,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji gasps]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:21.30,1:23:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:23.48,1:23:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No, wait!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:25.13,1:23:26.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[coughs]\NWhere’s Donloe?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:27.22,1:23:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Donloe!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:28.31,1:23:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,We got to go!\N[coughing]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:31.79,1:23:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:39.32,1:23:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting]
Dialogue: 0,1:24:11.13,1:24:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,[Bledsoe]\NThe coordinates you wanted.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:13.74,1:24:16.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m afraid you’re\Non the wrong boat.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:16.40,1:24:19.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s 2,000 miles\Noff the Cape of Good Hope.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:19.62,1:24:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,On the other side of the world.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:21.71,1:24:23.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn near exactly.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:26.97,1:24:28.58,Default,,0,0,0,,"Exactly."
Dialogue: 0,1:24:40.47,1:24:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly the opposite.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.51,1:24:44.51,Default,,0,0,0,,In case the Russians\Nwere listening.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:45.12,1:24:46.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Very clever.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:47.56,1:24:48.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Officer of the Deck,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:48.74,1:24:50.66,Default,,0,0,0,,set a new course: 3-4-0.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:50.82,1:24:52.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[officer]\NRight 15 degrees rudder, steady on course 3-4-0.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:52.74,1:24:54.31,Default,,0,0,0,,[helmsman] Aye, sir.\NMy rudder is right 15.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:54.48,1:24:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Officer of the Deck,\Nsubmerged contact, bearing 1-0-0.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:58.14,1:24:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,On the edge of\Nour starboard baffles.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:00.14,1:25:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,On speaker.\NExhibiting tonals of a Russian Oscar II-class submarine.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:02.79,1:25:05.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief of the Watch,\Nstation the fire control tracking party silently.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:05.71,1:25:08.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[chief] Silently. Aye, sir.\NWell, that’s one mission accomplished.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:08.41,1:25:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,We found the {\i1}Belgorod.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:25:10.06,1:25:11.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s right on our ass.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:11.32,1:25:13.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Wherever your mission\Nis taking you,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:14.15,1:25:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,now you’re taking\Nthe Russians there.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:18.46,1:25:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,No, they’re never gonna\Nknow my destination.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:20.77,1:25:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,When we reach those\Ncoordinates, I’d like you to slow to ten knots,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:23.16,1:25:24.68,Default,,0,0,0,,turn this boat around
Dialogue: 0,1:25:24.86,1:25:27.78,Default,,0,0,0,,and take the Russians\Nback the way we came.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:27.95,1:25:29.56,Default,,0,0,0,,What happens to\Nyour mission then?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:30.47,1:25:32.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ll be getting\Noff at the turn.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:34.22,1:25:35.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Mister,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:36.00,1:25:39.35,Default,,0,0,0,,without our decompression\Nchamber, you’ll die for sure.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:39.53,1:25:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, your decompression chamber\Nwas never part of our plan.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:47.62,1:25:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:49.41,1:25:50.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:52.58,1:25:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,What exactly is your plan?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:01.59,1:26:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace sighs]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:09.43,1:26:10.61,Default,,0,0,0,,[rattling]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:10.77,1:26:11.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[lid creaks]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:16.56,1:26:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:30.23,1:26:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:33.23,1:26:34.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] Huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:34.67,1:26:36.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:38.15,1:26:41.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Me? No! No, no, I can’t.\NI don’t know how. I don’t know how.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:41.20,1:26:43.20,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaking Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:48.86,1:26:50.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:51.12,1:26:52.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:53.34,1:26:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Show me.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:55.99,1:26:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:57.43,1:26:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s "left."
Dialogue: 0,1:26:59.00,1:27:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]\N[Grace repeats]
Dialogue: 0,1:27:01.39,1:27:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]\N[Grace repeats]
Dialogue: 0,1:27:08.92,1:27:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,"Forward."
Dialogue: 0,1:27:11.92,1:27:14.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Wooh.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:14.62,1:27:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] On this?\N"Wooh" is stop?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:17.54,1:27:19.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Wooh.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:21.28,1:27:22.28,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:23.59,1:27:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs] What’s this for?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:28.63,1:27:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:27:34.51,1:27:35.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[imitates growling]
Dialogue: 0,1:27:36.56,1:27:37.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Polar bear?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.64,1:27:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut,\Nimitates gunshot]
Dialogue: 0,1:27:47.70,1:27:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:27:59.40,1:28:01.40,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace shouts in Inuktitut]
Dialogue: 0,1:28:06.59,1:28:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,[continues shouting]
Dialogue: 0,1:28:15.94,1:28:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s your key, okay?\NPower on.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:19.47,1:28:20.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a deep breath.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:20.60,1:28:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[respirator hisses]
Dialogue: 0,1:28:22.65,1:28:25.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The Mark VII’s guidance\Nsystem will take you to your coordinates.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:25.39,1:28:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The depth at your\Nlocation is 500 feet.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:28.87,1:28:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Figure 19 minutes to your\Ntarget, 10 minutes on task.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:32.26,1:28:33.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember:
Dialogue: 0,1:28:33.53,1:28:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Any longer than that
Dialogue: 0,1:28:35.14,1:28:38.01,Default,,0,0,0,,and your chances of survival\Ndecrease by the second.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:38.18,1:28:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And don’t forget:
Dialogue: 0,1:28:39.92,1:28:42.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You must exhale continuously\Nas you rise to the surface.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:42.80,1:28:45.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold your breath\Nand your lungs will explode.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:45.84,1:28:48.10,Default,,0,0,0,,The VHF transmitter\Nyou asked for.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:48.28,1:28:51.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Your team should be\Nable to locate you within a two-mile radius.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:51.80,1:28:53.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Look after that.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:55.11,1:28:56.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:05.60,1:29:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Take care of my suit.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:10.82,1:29:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,[hatch opens]
Dialogue: 0,1:29:18.00,1:29:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,[hatch closes]
Dialogue: 0,1:29:20.22,1:29:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,[metallic straining]
Dialogue: 0,1:29:26.01,1:29:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Sonar, range to {\i1}Belgorod.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:28.45,1:29:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, I have near-field effect.\NToo close to tell.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:31.06,1:29:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Maneuvering, slow\Nto ten knots by log.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:33.63,1:29:35.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Helm, on my mark,\Nright full rudder.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:35.54,1:29:36.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Standing by\Nfor your mark, Captain.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:37.98,1:29:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales]
Dialogue: 0,1:29:47.03,1:29:48.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[rumbling, metallic thud]
Dialogue: 0,1:29:53.69,1:29:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,[respirator hisses]\N[breathing deeply]
Dialogue: 0,1:30:21.55,1:30:23.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling]
Dialogue: 0,1:30:36.08,1:30:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Mark the turn.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:37.34,1:30:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Aye, sir.\NMy rudder is right full.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:46.40,1:30:47.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:30:49.75,1:30:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Godspeed, mister.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:53.27,1:30:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales]
Dialogue: 0,1:30:55.97,1:30:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:30:58.89,1:31:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling]
Dialogue: 0,1:31:19.00,1:31:21.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:31:21.95,1:31:23.52,Default,,0,0,0,,[respirator hisses]
Dialogue: 0,1:31:54.25,1:31:56.30,Default,,0,0,0,,[rumbling intensifies]
Dialogue: 0,1:31:56.47,1:31:57.73,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:31:59.47,1:32:00.78,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:32:05.74,1:32:08.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhaling]
Dialogue: 0,1:32:15.44,1:32:17.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales]
Dialogue: 0,1:32:39.29,1:32:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,1:33:36.18,1:33:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:33:45.79,1:33:47.66,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:34:33.32,1:34:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:34:37.63,1:34:38.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:35:14.71,1:35:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:35:34.73,1:35:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling]
Dialogue: 0,1:35:48.57,1:35:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:36:11.72,1:36:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting]
Dialogue: 0,1:36:17.95,1:36:20.60,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting]
Dialogue: 0,1:36:41.67,1:36:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling, thudding]
Dialogue: 0,1:36:45.80,1:36:48.80,Default,,0,0,0,,[rumbling intensifies]
Dialogue: 0,1:37:06.12,1:37:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales]
Dialogue: 0,1:37:11.22,1:37:12.57,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,1:37:24.71,1:37:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[no audible dialogue]
Dialogue: 0,1:37:37.16,1:37:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,[water rushing]
Dialogue: 0,1:37:40.46,1:37:42.42,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales]
Dialogue: 0,1:37:45.56,1:37:47.00,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:37:49.30,1:37:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts echoing]
Dialogue: 0,1:38:01.40,1:38:04.14,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling]\N[gasping]
Dialogue: 0,1:38:13.50,1:38:15.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:38:28.86,1:38:30.91,Default,,0,0,0,,[heavy thud]
Dialogue: 0,1:38:36.04,1:38:38.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts, pants]
Dialogue: 0,1:39:09.25,1:39:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,[respirator hisses]
Dialogue: 0,1:39:18.39,1:39:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling]
Dialogue: 0,1:39:20.82,1:39:22.78,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,1:39:33.71,1:39:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling continues]
Dialogue: 0,1:39:40.15,1:39:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,[air hisses]\N[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:39:48.33,1:39:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:39:52.64,1:39:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[rumbling intensifies]
Dialogue: 0,1:40:13.27,1:40:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping, grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:40:25.85,1:40:27.59,Default,,0,0,0,,[labored breathing]
Dialogue: 0,1:40:46.82,1:40:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:40:51.57,1:40:52.61,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:41:20.07,1:41:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:41:29.56,1:41:30.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:41:34.52,1:41:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:41:36.96,1:41:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[respirator hisses]
Dialogue: 0,1:41:40.22,1:41:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts, strains]
Dialogue: 0,1:41:54.76,1:41:56.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Torpedo tube.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:08.64,1:42:10.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:42:32.10,1:42:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:42:37.98,1:42:39.98,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling continues]
Dialogue: 0,1:42:56.69,1:42:59.30,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps, grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:43:11.88,1:43:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:43:22.98,1:43:24.42,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:43:27.85,1:43:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting echoes]
Dialogue: 0,1:43:37.95,1:43:40.78,Default,,0,0,0,,[panting, grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:43:58.45,1:44:00.45,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts, gasping]
Dialogue: 0,1:44:05.37,1:44:10.16,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,1:44:13.03,1:44:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping, shivering]
Dialogue: 0,1:44:19.17,1:44:20.30,Default,,0,0,0,,[shivering]
Dialogue: 0,1:44:29.48,1:44:30.87,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:44:34.40,1:44:35.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:44:49.41,1:44:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:44:52.07,1:44:54.16,Default,,0,0,0,,[groaning]
Dialogue: 0,1:44:58.99,1:45:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:45:01.34,1:45:03.30,Default,,0,0,0,,[deep rumbling continues]
Dialogue: 0,1:45:10.00,1:45:12.70,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts, shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:45:20.84,1:45:23.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:45:34.11,1:45:35.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,1:45:44.99,1:45:46.21,Default,,0,0,0,,[inhaling forcefully]
Dialogue: 0,1:46:28.38,1:46:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,[muffled strained grunts]
Dialogue: 0,1:47:43.59,1:47:46.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[no audible dialogue]
Dialogue: 0,1:48:47.35,1:48:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s okay. It’s okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:52.35,1:48:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,1:49:00.14,1:49:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is it?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:01.62,1:49:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The Podkova, where is it?\NHere.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:06.71,1:49:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You did it, Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:09.46,1:49:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You did it.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:14.90,1:49:16.55,Default,,0,0,0,,So what happens now?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:20.47,1:49:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Now...
Dialogue: 0,1:49:22.38,1:49:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,we find Gabriel.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:26.08,1:49:28.43,Default,,0,0,0,,We get Luther’s poison pill.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:29.78,1:49:31.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And we kill the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:33.35,1:49:35.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan, I’ve been thinking.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:36.35,1:49:39.88,Default,,0,0,0,,How can we undo everything\Nthe Entity has done?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:40.05,1:49:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,If we could control it,
Dialogue: 0,1:49:42.92,1:49:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,maybe we could bring\Nthe world back from the brink.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:48.10,1:49:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Grace...
Dialogue: 0,1:49:50.67,1:49:55.20,Default,,0,0,0,,who on earth would you ever\Ntrust with that much power?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:55.37,1:49:57.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you, of course.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:57.94,1:50:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Only you.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:00.64,1:50:03.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe you were\Nmeant to do this.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:04.42,1:50:05.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Not me.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:06.47,1:50:07.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Not anyone.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:14.52,1:50:15.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you...
Dialogue: 0,1:50:18.31,1:50:20.40,Default,,0,0,0,,for bringing me back.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:21.88,1:50:23.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing to it.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:25.40,1:50:26.79,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,1:50:35.80,1:50:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a long story.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:43.11,1:50:45.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[airplane roars]
Dialogue: 0,1:51:08.31,1:51:10.84,Default,,0,0,0,,We haven’t been\Nformally introduced. I’m--
Dialogue: 0,1:51:11.01,1:51:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,William Donloe. Langley.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:13.97,1:51:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,We met thirty years ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:16.28,1:51:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Almost.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:51:23.07,1:51:24.51,Default,,0,0,0,,So you’re him.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:24.68,1:51:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand I owe you my life.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:29.55,1:51:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t know how to make amends\Nfor what I’ve done to yours.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:32.38,1:51:35.60,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s a matter of\Nperspective, friend.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:35.78,1:51:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,If you hadn’t broken\Nin the vault 30 years ago, I’d probably still be there.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:40.52,1:51:43.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I’d probably even\Nthink I was happy.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:43.26,1:51:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I never would have found\Nthe only home that’s ever brought me peace.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:47.88,1:51:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And I certainly never would\Nhave met the woman I love.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:57.45,1:51:59.63,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s nothing\Nto be sorry about.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:02.93,1:52:04.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I owe you my life.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:15.03,1:52:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] We’ll be landing\Njust as the clock runs out.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:17.17,1:52:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,By the time we arrive,\Nthe Entity will have control
Dialogue: 0,1:52:19.17,1:52:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,of the world’s nine\Nautomated doomsday arsenals.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:21.78,1:52:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And it will be fueling\Nthe missiles it controls.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:24.09,1:52:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,But it can’t launch until\Nit has a safe place to hide if it wants to survive.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:28.65,1:52:30.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The safest place is here.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:30.57,1:52:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,What is that?\NThe Doomsday Vault. Kongo Yowa.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:33.75,1:52:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[Donloe] It’s a top secret\Nstandalone, solar-powered,
Dialogue: 0,1:52:37.27,1:52:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}TEMPEST-hardened, Level A{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:52:39.23,1:52:40.88,Default,,0,0,0,,exabyte data server.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:41.06,1:52:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,One billion\Ngigabytes of storage.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:43.19,1:52:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s a lot of home movies.\N[Donloe] Well, you’re not far off.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:45.76,1:52:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It contains all\Nthe accumulated knowledge deemed worthy of preservation.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:48.98,1:52:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And it’s fully shielded.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:51.03,1:52:52.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}Totally impervious {\i0}\N{\i1}to electromagnetic energy {\i0} {\i1}of any kind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:52:53.11,1:52:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No transmissions in or out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:52:54.64,1:52:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,[Donloe] {\i1}An incorruptible {\i0}\N{\i1}ark of human history{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:52:56.81,1:52:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,built to survive\Nthe end of the world.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:58.68,1:53:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,So, if the Entity got in there,
Dialogue: 0,1:53:00.95,1:53:03.13,Default,,0,0,0,,it could survive for\Nthousands of years,
Dialogue: 0,1:53:03.30,1:53:04.87,Default,,0,0,0,,no matter what happened\Nto the rest of the world.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:05.04,1:53:06.69,Default,,0,0,0,,[Degas] And why would it\Nwant to survive?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:06.87,1:53:09.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What does it stand\Nto gain from wiping out all life on Earth?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:09.70,1:53:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,A question Noah and his family\Nmust have asked just before the flood.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:13.79,1:53:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] The Anti-God\Nthinks it’s God.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:15.92,1:53:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] How do we kill it?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:17.40,1:53:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Always
Dialogue: 0,1:53:18.97,1:53:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,right to the point,\Naren’t you?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:20.66,1:53:24.62,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the poison pill\Ncontaining Luther’s algorithm.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:25.93,1:53:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,And this is the Podkova,
Dialogue: 0,1:53:27.71,1:53:29.76,Default,,0,0,0,,containing the Entity’s\Noriginal source code.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:29.93,1:53:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,When combined, they will\Nform a sort of digital toxin.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:33.68,1:53:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,When uploaded to cyberspace,\Nthis toxin will attack the Entity
Dialogue: 0,1:53:36.55,1:53:39.03,Default,,0,0,0,,and alter its ability\Nto perceive reality.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:39.20,1:53:41.94,Default,,0,0,0,,So, combine that\Nwith the Podkova...
Dialogue: 0,1:53:42.12,1:53:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,We can deceive\Nthe Lord of Lies.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:45.30,1:53:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] But...
Dialogue: 0,1:53:47.34,1:53:48.65,Default,,0,0,0,,...there’s always a but.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:48.82,1:53:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mais...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:53:50.26,1:53:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,we don’t have\NLuther’s poison pill.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:51.78,1:53:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Gabriel does.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:54.04,1:53:56.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Which is why we can be sure\Nhe’ll be waiting for us in the Doomsday Vault.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:56.87,1:53:59.92,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji]\NOnce the Entity is infected with Luther’s algorithm,
Dialogue: 0,1:54:00.09,1:54:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,it will think it’s entering the\Njunction’s central data server
Dialogue: 0,1:54:02.79,1:54:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,when it will actually\Nbe going here.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:06.01,1:54:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:07.71,1:54:09.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Careful,\Nit’s very delicate.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:09.80,1:54:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It can’t be.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:12.58,1:54:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a 5D optical data drive.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:15.37,1:54:17.68,Default,,0,0,0,,360 terabytes in\Nthe palm of your hand.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:17.85,1:54:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,[Donloe] I thought these\Nwere just theoretical.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:19.81,1:54:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] They were.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:20.98,1:54:22.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Until Luther built one.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:27.86,1:54:30.25,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Entity is our genie,
Dialogue: 0,1:54:30.43,1:54:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,then this optical drive is\Nthe bottle we’ll capture it in.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:34.43,1:54:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Which brings us\Nto the tricky part.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:36.35,1:54:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Once inside,
Dialogue: 0,1:54:38.35,1:54:40.05,Default,,0,0,0,,once it believes\Nthat it’s safe,
Dialogue: 0,1:54:40.22,1:54:42.88,Default,,0,0,0,,the Entity will\Ninitiate a nuclear launch.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:43.05,1:54:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,We have to disconnect this\Ndrive before it can do that.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:45.92,1:54:47.10,Default,,0,0,0,,How long do we have?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:47.92,1:54:48.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Roughly...
Dialogue: 0,1:54:49.01,1:54:50.45,Default,,0,0,0,,[both] 100 milliseconds.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:50.62,1:54:52.36,Default,,0,0,0,,The blink of an eye.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:52.54,1:54:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] If we do it too soon...
Dialogue: 0,1:54:54.54,1:54:56.19,Default,,0,0,0,,We won’t trap the\Ngenie in the bottle.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:56.37,1:54:58.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm. And if\Nwe do it too late...
Dialogue: 0,1:54:58.33,1:55:00.51,Default,,0,0,0,,We won’t prevent the Entity\Nfrom launching.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:00.68,1:55:02.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Either way...
Dialogue: 0,1:55:02.37,1:55:04.02,Default,,0,0,0,,[Donloe] {\i1}If we pull the{\i0}\N{\i1}drive at the wrong time,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:55:04.20,1:55:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,the Entity wins.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:05.86,1:55:07.43,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:07.60,1:55:10.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang on. If the Doomsday Vault\Nis electronically shielded,
Dialogue: 0,1:55:10.90,1:55:12.34,Default,,0,0,0,,how does the Entity\Nexpect to get in?
Dialogue: 0,1:55:12.51,1:55:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It expects us to let it in.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:15.34,1:55:18.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like Gabriel expects me\Nto hand over the Podkova.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:18.56,1:55:20.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither of which\Nwe’d ever do, obviously.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:22.00,1:55:23.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,1:55:23.66,1:55:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Think about it. The vault\Nis electronically shielded.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:26.05,1:55:28.44,Default,,0,0,0,,No signals get in or out.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:28.62,1:55:31.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone has to go\Noutside the vault
Dialogue: 0,1:55:31.36,1:55:35.41,Default,,0,0,0,,in order to upload Luther’s\Npoison pill to the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:35.58,1:55:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,And if Gabriel wants\Nto control the Entity...
Dialogue: 0,1:55:39.41,1:55:42.89,Default,,0,0,0,,He has to upload\NLuther’s poison pill.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:44.46,1:55:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re not seriously\Ngonna give him the Podkova
Dialogue: 0,1:55:47.68,1:55:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and let him get\Naway with the pill.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:49.55,1:55:52.34,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s exactly\Nwhat I’m going to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:52.51,1:55:55.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Gabriel will be part of {\i0}\N{\i1}the team and never know it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:55:55.86,1:55:58.95,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s insane! You’re letting\Nthe Entity into the vault.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:59.13,1:56:01.09,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s precisely what\Nit wants you to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:01.26,1:56:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,"It is written."
Dialogue: 0,1:56:03.70,1:56:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:05.00,1:56:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,And it’s the only\Nchance we have
Dialogue: 0,1:56:07.00,1:56:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,of beating Gabriel\Nand the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:08.35,1:56:09.61,Default,,0,0,0,,One chance in a trillion.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:09.79,1:56:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan, think about\Nwhat you’re doing.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:12.05,1:56:15.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Think about how you got here.\NThink about how the world got here.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:15.75,1:56:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you know that\Nthe Entity didn’t want you to recover the Podkova?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:19.36,1:56:20.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe it told you\Nit was impossible
Dialogue: 0,1:56:21.10,1:56:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,because it knew that was the\Nthing that you needed to hear!
Dialogue: 0,1:56:25.02,1:56:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers] Is that\Nwhat you think, Grace?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:26.85,1:56:29.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you’re risking\Nthe fate of the world
Dialogue: 0,1:56:29.98,1:56:32.24,Default,,0,0,0,,and billions of lives
Dialogue: 0,1:56:32.42,1:56:33.99,Default,,0,0,0,,on the blink of an eye.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:34.16,1:56:35.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan whispering] Yes, Grace.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:35.64,1:56:36.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I am.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:38.47,1:56:41.26,Default,,0,0,0,,And if there was\Nanother choice, I’d take it.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:42.65,1:56:45.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you all have your\Ndoubts. I don’t blame you.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:45.78,1:56:47.74,Default,,0,0,0,,But we have to stick together.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:47.91,1:56:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,And we have to\Nmake sure that Grace
Dialogue: 0,1:56:50.48,1:56:53.22,Default,,0,0,0,,is the one to\Ndisconnect that drive.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:53.40,1:56:55.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Me?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:55.36,1:56:59.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What separates a good\Npickpocket from a great one?
Dialogue: 0,1:57:00.10,1:57:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,1:57:03.58,1:57:04.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Timing.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:05.71,1:57:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Blink of an eye.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:38.96,1:57:40.75,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] {\i1}Where is everybody?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:57:40.92,1:57:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,They know what’s coming.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:43.88,1:57:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,They’ve all gone home.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:50.89,1:57:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,[gun clicks]
Dialogue: 0,1:58:52.56,1:58:56.43,Default,,0,0,0,,[Angstrom] We can’t\Naccurately predict how fast the Entity is moving now.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:56.61,1:58:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President, Hunt is gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:59.26,1:59:01.52,Default,,0,0,0,,If he isn’t dead,\Nthe Russians have him.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:01.70,1:59:03.66,Default,,0,0,0,,If we lose\Ncontrol of our arsenal,
Dialogue: 0,1:59:03.83,1:59:06.27,Default,,0,0,0,,we lose any hope of preventing\Nthe Entity from launching.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:06.44,1:59:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,We are out of time!
Dialogue: 0,1:59:12.23,1:59:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,General Sidney...
Dialogue: 0,1:59:14.80,1:59:17.33,Default,,0,0,0,,what is our most\Nlimited attack option?
Dialogue: 0,1:59:17.50,1:59:19.20,Default,,0,0,0,,[Sidney] Surgical\Nnuclear strikes
Dialogue: 0,1:59:19.37,1:59:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,confined strictly to\Nthe command centers of the eight nations
Dialogue: 0,1:59:22.50,1:59:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,under the Entity’s control.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:24.20,1:59:27.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Beijing. Islamabad. London.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:27.99,1:59:31.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Moscow. New Delhi. Paris.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:31.38,1:59:33.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Pyongyang. And Tel Aviv.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:34.08,1:59:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Casualties.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:35.99,1:59:39.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Estimated death tolls\Nfrom initial strikes.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:40.65,1:59:45.70,Default,,0,0,0,,And more later, of course,\Nfrom the resulting nuclear fallout.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:45.87,1:59:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Estimates, uh... vary.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:49.18,1:59:53.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Obviously the bombing\Nof major cities in eight different countries
Dialogue: 0,1:59:53.36,1:59:56.10,Default,,0,0,0,,would create an unprecedented\Npolitical crisis.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:56.28,2:00:00.55,Default,,0,0,0,,One that would likely lead\Nto a protracted global war.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:00.72,2:00:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It may be diplomatically\Nprudent to make a...
Dialogue: 0,2:00:06.33,2:00:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,gesture.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:09.38,2:00:11.12,Default,,0,0,0,,A gesture?
Dialogue: 0,2:00:11.29,2:00:14.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Sacrifice one of our\Ncities here at home.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:15.51,2:00:17.60,Default,,0,0,0,,We’ve prepared a list.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:19.73,2:00:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,[Angstrom] Cities have been\Narranged by strategic and economic importance.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:24.09,2:00:26.31,Default,,0,0,0,,And... [clears throat]
Dialogue: 0,2:00:26.48,2:00:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,...population, of course.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:28.09,2:00:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You’d be sacrificing\Na hundred million lives...
Dialogue: 0,2:00:32.49,2:00:34.45,Default,,0,0,0,,to save seven billion.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:36.23,2:00:37.97,Default,,0,0,0,,This can’t be happening.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:38.14,2:00:39.36,Default,,0,0,0,,[Sidney] Madam President,
Dialogue: 0,2:00:39.54,2:00:42.24,Default,,0,0,0,,we are in\Nthe Entity’s reality now.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:42.41,2:00:45.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And this is checkmate.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:51.77,2:00:52.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[stomps]
Dialogue: 0,2:01:02.52,2:01:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Gunnery Sergeant,\NI need your sidearm.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:06.52,2:01:07.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir?
Dialogue: 0,2:01:08.00,2:01:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You heard me, son.\NHand it over.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:25.71,2:01:27.80,Default,,0,0,0,,The main server’s\Nthrough there.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:27.98,2:01:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Benji, Grace,\Nyou come with me.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:31.33,2:01:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The rest of you,\Nyou just wait here.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:33.16,2:01:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Non.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:01:34.42,2:01:35.68,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French]\NGabriel is down there.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:36.33,2:01:37.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me come with you.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:38.73,2:01:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,His time will come.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:42.47,2:01:43.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[speaks French]
Dialogue: 0,2:01:45.65,2:01:47.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[footsteps splashing]
Dialogue: 0,2:02:04.23,2:02:06.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s the door\Nto the server room.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:06.45,2:02:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s too exposed.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:08.45,2:02:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You should go back\Nto the others.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:10.58,2:02:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,If Gabriel is in there,\Nhe’ll kill you.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:13.67,2:02:16.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He has to leave here with\Nthe pill and the Podkova.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:17.72,2:02:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m expendable.\NNeither of you are.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:21.64,2:02:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s right.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:32.52,2:02:34.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Take care of your team.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:22.70,2:03:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel] Your final reckoning!
Dialogue: 0,2:03:44.07,2:03:45.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Thirty megaton yield.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:46.11,2:03:50.20,Default,,0,0,0,,My man lets go of that\Nbutton and the Entity has no place to hide.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:50.38,2:03:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And what happens to you?
Dialogue: 0,2:03:52.43,2:03:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a plane that’ll take me\Nto minimum safe distance.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:56.34,2:04:00.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Reliable, analog,\Nunder the radar.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:00.26,2:04:03.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I even brought a spare.\NJust in case.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:03.52,2:04:05.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And you honestly believe\Ndestroying this place
Dialogue: 0,2:04:06.05,2:04:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,will stop the Entity\Nfrom launching.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:07.70,2:04:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it’s bluffing.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:09.35,2:04:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It won’t end the world\Nif it can’t survive,
Dialogue: 0,2:04:11.27,2:04:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,and it can’t survive\Nif you don’t let it in.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:13.45,2:04:15.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Now hand over the Podkova
Dialogue: 0,2:04:15.58,2:04:17.06,Default,,0,0,0,,and I’ll let you walk away.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:17.23,2:04:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would I believe that?\NBecause I want you
Dialogue: 0,2:04:20.50,2:04:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,and everyone you care about
Dialogue: 0,2:04:23.02,2:04:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,to live long lives\Nin the world I create
Dialogue: 0,2:04:26.33,2:04:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,when the Entity answers to me.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:28.81,2:04:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re beat, Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:30.51,2:04:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,If not today, some other place,\Nsome other time.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:35.34,2:04:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as I have this,
Dialogue: 0,2:04:37.60,2:04:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,wherever I go, you will follow.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:40.78,2:04:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,And the Podkova\Nwill come to me.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:43.48,2:04:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,That is written.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:45.43,2:04:47.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing is written.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:47.70,2:04:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m not sure\NLuther would agree.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:52.70,2:04:53.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Now,
Dialogue: 0,2:04:54.14,2:04:56.53,Default,,0,0,0,,tell me I win!
Dialogue: 0,2:05:06.76,2:05:07.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You win.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:07.89,2:05:09.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I like the sound of that.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:10.55,2:05:12.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Say it again.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:12.20,2:05:13.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh-uh.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:13.29,2:05:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:14.81,2:05:16.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Hands where I can\Nsee them, dickhead.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:19.90,2:05:21.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,2:05:49.67,2:05:51.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Let’s have it.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:51.33,2:05:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Time?
Dialogue: 0,2:05:52.55,2:05:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,18 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:55.20,2:05:56.38,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,2:05:58.77,2:05:59.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:59.94,2:06:01.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Donloe.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:01.38,2:06:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,William Donloe.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:02.86,2:06:05.04,Default,,0,0,0,,My wife, Tapeesa.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:05.21,2:06:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I got to hand it to you, Hunt.\NThis is one crackerjack unit you’ve put together.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:09.08,2:06:13.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m imagining the Entity is\Nshaking in its virtual shorts right about now.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:13.44,2:06:17.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What do I need to know\Nabout this, and what exactly was the play?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:17.44,2:06:20.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The only play is\Nto give that to him, and let him go right now.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:20.75,2:06:23.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You want me to give this\Nto him and let him go.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:23.40,2:06:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] Right now.\N[Kittridge] Right now.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:24.93,2:06:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now.\NRight now...
Dialogue: 0,2:06:27.14,2:06:29.01,Default,,0,0,0,,the President of\Nthe United States
Dialogue: 0,2:06:29.19,2:06:31.85,Default,,0,0,0,,is preparing to\Nvaporize millions upon millions of souls.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:32.02,2:06:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,All because Ethan here\Ndoesn’t believe that anyone can safely control the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:37.59,2:06:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Does that sound sane?\NTo anyone?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:40.51,2:06:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe you should ask\Nthe crew of the {\i1}Sevastopol.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:06:45.90,2:06:47.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Time?\N17 minutes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:47.95,2:06:50.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Kittridge.\NYou wouldn’t be here if Ethan didn’t have a plan.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:51.08,2:06:53.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Whomever tells me\Nwhat that plan is
Dialogue: 0,2:06:53.69,2:06:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,will be sparing millions\Nof lives, and you’ll be spared the fate of the others.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:57.57,2:06:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, we’re running out of time.\NWe need to get to a minimum safe distance.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:59.96,2:07:01.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are we still standing here?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:01.35,2:07:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Because he’s here\Nand he’s here.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:04.27,2:07:06.62,Default,,0,0,0,,And this means something.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:07.32,2:07:08.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Any second now
Dialogue: 0,2:07:08.97,2:07:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan’s gonna\Ntell me what it is.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:11.93,2:07:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ve known this man\Nfor a long time.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:14.63,2:07:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,And he won’t want anything to\Nhappen to his precious team.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:24.33,2:07:26.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And that’s the pattern,\Nisn’t it?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:26.99,2:07:29.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You refuse to sacrifice
Dialogue: 0,2:07:30.12,2:07:32.60,Default,,0,0,0,,the ones you hold close.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:34.86,2:07:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,That is why we’re still here.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:38.22,2:07:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s over.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:39.70,2:07:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s no shame in it.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:41.87,2:07:42.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Now just...
Dialogue: 0,2:07:44.00,2:07:45.35,Default,,0,0,0,,tell me what I’m missing.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:45.96,2:07:46.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers] Time.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:02.33,2:08:03.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.\NNow!
Dialogue: 0,2:08:04.15,2:08:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,[gunfire]
Dialogue: 0,2:08:12.77,2:08:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping, grunting]
Dialogue: 0,2:08:20.30,2:08:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Gabriel!
Dialogue: 0,2:08:24.70,2:08:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Paris, Gabriel now!\NKill him now!
Dialogue: 0,2:08:27.74,2:08:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine revs]
Dialogue: 0,2:08:29.22,2:08:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[clicks]
Dialogue: 0,2:08:31.92,2:08:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Degas! Gabriel! Shoot him,\Nshoot him, kill him! Kill him!
Dialogue: 0,2:08:37.41,2:08:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Catch me if you can, Ethan!
Dialogue: 0,2:08:39.45,2:08:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You go after him\Nand get the pill.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:41.37,2:08:43.11,Default,,0,0,0,,We’ll get to the server room\Nand let the Entity in.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:43.28,2:08:44.28,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales]
Dialogue: 0,2:08:47.20,2:08:48.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan, we’ll figure it out.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:49.07,2:08:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You are forgetting the bomb.\NThe nuclear bomb.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:51.77,2:08:53.42,Default,,0,0,0,,We’ll figure it out.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:53.60,2:08:54.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan!Benji.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:54.81,2:08:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Go! I got this.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:56.38,2:08:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Go.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:01.21,2:09:02.47,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers] Blink of an eye.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:08.57,2:09:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ethan] Paris! Cover, cover!
Dialogue: 0,2:09:13.35,2:09:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Hunt!
Dialogue: 0,2:09:17.84,2:09:20.76,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans] I thought\Nhe’d never leave.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:24.80,2:09:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We’ll figure it out.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:27.24,2:09:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine revs]
Dialogue: 0,2:09:33.72,2:09:34.85,Default,,0,0,0,,We got to go, Briggs.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:35.03,2:09:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s your funeral.\NLet’s go.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:54.26,2:09:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[laughs]
Dialogue: 0,2:10:21.64,2:10:23.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[thudding]
Dialogue: 0,2:10:28.91,2:10:33.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping, grunting]
Dialogue: 0,2:11:24.53,2:11:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine roars]
Dialogue: 0,2:11:38.33,2:11:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunting]
Dialogue: 0,2:11:58.21,2:11:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,There has to be\Na way to disarm it.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:00.09,2:12:01.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if you can prevent it\Nfrom going nuclear,
Dialogue: 0,2:12:01.74,2:12:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,you can’t stop those\Ndetonators from exploding.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:04.00,2:12:05.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Could we survive the blast\Nfrom the server room?
Dialogue: 0,2:12:05.96,2:12:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Only if someone stays behind\Nand stops the bomb from going critical.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:09.10,2:12:12.89,Default,,0,0,0,,But whoever that is,\Nthey’re not going to make it.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:14.01,2:12:16.80,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] Who will live\Nand who will die?
Dialogue: 0,2:12:19.93,2:12:23.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We’ll handle the bomb.\NThe rest of you get Benji to the server room.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:23.81,2:12:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s no time\Nto discuss it. Go.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:26.42,2:12:27.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[in Inuktitut]\NI will see you again.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:28.07,2:12:29.33,Default,,0,0,0,,[both sigh]
Dialogue: 0,2:12:31.60,2:12:32.86,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Keep pressure on it.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:33.03,2:12:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] I’ve got it.\NI’ve got it.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:36.82,2:12:38.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ll stay with them.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:38.47,2:12:41.43,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s nothing for me\Nto do in the server room.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:42.00,2:12:43.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:44.65,2:12:45.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:50.24,2:13:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:14:13.52,2:14:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,[drill whirs]
Dialogue: 0,2:14:15.09,2:14:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Where’d you learn to do this?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:16.48,2:14:18.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Never said I did.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:21.18,2:14:22.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji grunting]
Dialogue: 0,2:14:32.54,2:14:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans]
Dialogue: 0,2:14:35.59,2:14:36.94,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,2:14:37.11,2:14:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not good.\NWhat is it?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:39.51,2:14:41.86,Default,,0,0,0,,If I had to guess,\Nit’s a tension pneumothorax.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:42.03,2:14:45.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What does that mean?\NPressure building in the pleural cavity. [gasps]
Dialogue: 0,2:14:45.56,2:14:47.26,Default,,0,0,0,,My lung is collapsing.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:47.43,2:14:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,If we don’t act fast, it means\Nsuffocation or cardiac arrest.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:51.21,2:14:53.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Do either of you have\Nany medical experience?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:54.91,2:14:56.04,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] I kill people.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:57.31,2:14:58.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I can work with that.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:58.79,2:15:00.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping] Grace, I need\Nyou to hack the server
Dialogue: 0,2:15:00.61,2:15:02.22,Default,,0,0,0,,so we can let the Entity in.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:02.40,2:15:04.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Grab the tools, head\Nto the panel. Paris.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:04.84,2:15:05.93,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French]\NYou have to operate on me.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:06.10,2:15:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Moi?{\i0}\N[Benji speaking French]
Dialogue: 0,2:15:08.45,2:15:10.93,Default,,0,0,0,,[in English] First I need you\Nto plug the bullet hole, make it airtight.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:11.10,2:15:12.14,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] Close it tight.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:12.32,2:15:13.41,Default,,0,0,0,,A bandage.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:13.58,2:15:14.49,Default,,0,0,0,,A bandage please.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:16.72,2:15:18.07,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:15:18.24,2:15:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,[groaning, gasps]
Dialogue: 0,2:15:44.57,2:15:45.70,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,2:16:10.81,2:16:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m in. What do I do?\N[groaning]
Dialogue: 0,2:16:12.90,2:16:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Grace, I need you to\Nfind the power switch...
Dialogue: 0,2:16:14.82,2:16:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps] ...to the server’s\Ninternal network.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:16.39,2:16:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Got it.\NParis.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:18.04,2:16:20.78,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] My clavicle...\Ncount down to my second rib.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:22.78,2:16:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now...
Dialogue: 0,2:16:24.52,2:16:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,...make an incision.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:33.40,2:16:34.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold this.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:35.23,2:16:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[inhales]\N[gasping]
Dialogue: 0,2:16:36.67,2:16:38.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Paris.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:38.19,2:16:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French]\NIt’s going to be OK.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:39.67,2:16:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans]
Dialogue: 0,2:16:41.19,2:16:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Bottoms up.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:43.89,2:16:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[muffled pained grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:16:48.42,2:16:50.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans]\NNow what?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:50.51,2:16:51.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Pen... in the bag.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:51.59,2:16:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Pressure.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:53.16,2:16:54.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Take it apart.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:54.68,2:16:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,[in English] Grace,\Ndid you find the switch?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:56.69,2:16:58.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N[Benji] Okay, shut it off.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:58.73,2:17:01.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] What next?\NOpen the panel.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:01.74,2:17:04.26,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] Now what?\N[in English] Push that into the incision.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:04.91,2:17:06.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:12.05,2:17:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,[inhales sharply]
Dialogue: 0,2:17:14.10,2:17:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps]\N[panting]
Dialogue: 0,2:17:15.88,2:17:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,[in French] Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:16.92,2:17:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasping]
Dialogue: 0,2:17:19.10,2:17:20.28,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,2:17:20.45,2:17:21.97,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers] Oh, thank God.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:22.15,2:17:23.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Degas, how’s it going in there?
Dialogue: 0,2:17:24.06,2:17:26.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, everything’s\Nunder control here.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:26.37,2:17:29.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, hold this very steady.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:29.42,2:17:32.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But don’t pull it out.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:40.95,2:17:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,[wind whipping]
Dialogue: 0,2:17:54.31,2:17:55.92,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel] {\i1}It’s like{\i0}\N{\i1}I said, Ethan.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:17:58.75,2:18:00.32,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as I have the pill...
Dialogue: 0,2:18:01.71,2:18:04.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the Podkova will come to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:18:06.71,2:18:09.06,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine sputters]\N[gasps]
Dialogue: 0,2:18:48.80,2:18:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[laughs]
Dialogue: 0,2:18:54.33,2:18:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang on.\NWhat? What is it?
Dialogue: 0,2:18:56.37,2:18:58.55,Default,,0,0,0,,We may have a way out of this.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:58.72,2:19:01.38,Default,,0,0,0,,These ground wires\Nare triple redundant.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:01.55,2:19:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,If we cut any three\Nof them simultaneously,
Dialogue: 0,2:19:03.90,2:19:06.43,Default,,0,0,0,,we could delay these\Ndetonators from exploding.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:06.60,2:19:08.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe long enough for someone\Nto make it to the server room.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:08.95,2:19:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,How long?
Dialogue: 0,2:19:11.39,2:19:13.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Ten seconds. Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:14.52,2:19:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You think you can make it\Nto that door in ten seconds?
Dialogue: 0,2:19:19.83,2:19:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Only one way to find out.\NHand me the ratchet.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:22.40,2:19:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, I’m in. What now?\N[Benji] We’re not out of the woods yet.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:25.75,2:19:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Any minute now,\Nmy blood pressure’s gonna drop drastically
Dialogue: 0,2:19:27.84,2:19:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,and I’ll grow faint,\Nso we need to work fast.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:31.06,2:19:34.32,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s a receiver in\Nthe tool bag. A silver box with two lights on it.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:34.50,2:19:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Got it.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:36.24,2:19:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,We need to splice that into\Nthe server’s solar panels
Dialogue: 0,2:19:37.59,2:19:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and make an antenna.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:38.67,2:19:39.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That way we’ll know
Dialogue: 0,2:19:40.11,2:19:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,when Ethan’s uploading\Nthe poison pill.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:41.72,2:19:43.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep. Got it.\NNow this is the really tricky part.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:43.85,2:19:46.20,Default,,0,0,0,,There is a bundle of blue,\Nblack, and red cables
Dialogue: 0,2:19:46.38,2:19:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,in the lower right corner.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:48.34,2:19:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. Walk me through it.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:50.34,2:19:52.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m gonna need you to\Ncut two of the wires in a specific order,
Dialogue: 0,2:19:53.12,2:19:57.12,Default,,0,0,0,,but whatever you do,\Ndo not cut...
Dialogue: 0,2:19:59.61,2:20:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Benji!\N[grunts] ...the red ones.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:03.57,2:20:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,[Serling] Madam President,\Nas your Secretary of Defense
Dialogue: 0,2:20:06.70,2:20:10.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I direct your attention\Nto CONPLAN 8044,
Dialogue: 0,2:20:10.58,2:20:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,selected Attack Option 9.1.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:13.36,2:20:15.93,Default,,0,0,0,,A targeted nuclear strike\Non the command centers
Dialogue: 0,2:20:16.10,2:20:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,of all eight nations now\Ncontrolled by the Entity.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:19.41,2:20:23.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Amended to include\Nthe American city you’ve chosen to sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:25.33,2:20:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The Biscuit.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:39.65,2:20:41.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you spoken to your son?
Dialogue: 0,2:20:43.48,2:20:45.44,Default,,0,0,0,,What would I tell him?
Dialogue: 0,2:20:45.61,2:20:47.66,Default,,0,0,0,,[Serling]\NAuthentication code verified.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:52.05,2:20:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,2:21:04.89,2:21:06.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Ethan.
Dialogue: 0,2:21:06.50,2:21:07.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Know when you’re beat.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:21:08.02,2:21:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Any minute now{\i0}\N{\i1}your team will be dead.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:21:10.64,2:21:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the Entity will{\i0}\N{\i1}have no place to hide.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:21:23.52,2:21:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,[rattling]
Dialogue: 0,2:21:27.87,2:21:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gabriel] {\i1}I’m gonna run{\i0}\N{\i1}you into the ground.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:21:30.00,2:21:32.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Podkova will be mine{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:21:32.66,2:21:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and the Entity{\i0}\N{\i1}will answer to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:21:35.49,2:21:37.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It’s only a matter of time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:21:39.40,2:21:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grace] Ow.\N[Degas] {\i1}Grace, we think{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:21:40.97,2:21:42.19,Default,,0,0,0,,we can prevent this bomb\Nfrom going nuclear,
Dialogue: 0,2:21:42.36,2:21:43.49,Default,,0,0,0,,but all of these\Ndetonators will explode.
Dialogue: 0,2:21:43.67,2:21:44.71,Default,,0,0,0,,How big a blast?
Dialogue: 0,2:21:45.67,2:21:47.24,Default,,0,0,0,,How big a blast are we talking?
Dialogue: 0,2:21:48.98,2:21:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,[Degas] {\i1}Big.{\i0}\N[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:21:50.63,2:21:52.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethan needs all the\Ntime we can give him.
Dialogue: 0,2:21:52.50,2:21:54.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not make the last cut\Nuntil we absolutely have to.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:01.03,2:22:02.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President,
Dialogue: 0,2:22:02.73,2:22:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,launch is now enabled.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:31.85,2:22:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,[breathing shakily]
Dialogue: 0,2:22:33.59,2:22:35.07,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,2:22:35.24,2:22:38.20,Default,,0,0,0,,What we should have done\Nin the first place.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:38.38,2:22:42.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Order U.S. Strategic Command\NCenter to cut their power.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:43.08,2:22:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Take our missiles\Noffline entirely.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:46.38,2:22:48.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Shut everything down.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:48.47,2:22:51.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President,\Nthat would leave the country completely defenseless.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:51.91,2:22:56.31,Default,,0,0,0,,But deny the Entity access\Nto the largest nuclear arsenal on Earth.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:56.48,2:22:57.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, make the call.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:57.96,2:22:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, thank God.
Dialogue: 0,2:22:59.40,2:23:00.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma’am, We are the only\Nnation on Earth
Dialogue: 0,2:23:01.09,2:23:03.05,Default,,0,0,0,,with the power\Nto attack the Entity!
Dialogue: 0,2:23:03.23,2:23:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And now we’re the only nation\Nin the world with the power of choice.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:05.88,2:23:07.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Today I choose not to attack.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:08.14,2:23:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President,\Nthink this through.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:09.89,2:23:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You are making\Na terrible mistake!
Dialogue: 0,2:23:11.93,2:23:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,For the sake of the country,\Nplease listen to reason.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:14.24,2:23:15.50,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s precisely\Nwhat I’m doing.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:15.67,2:23:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Connect me with\NStrategic Command HQ.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:18.07,2:23:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,[Serling] Millions\Nof people will die, ma’am, if you don’t push that button.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:20.50,2:23:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[Walters] And millions of other\Npeople will die if she does!
Dialogue: 0,2:23:22.42,2:23:24.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What give us the right to\Ndecide who lives and who dies?
Dialogue: 0,2:23:24.38,2:23:26.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[Serling] She took an oath as\NPresident of the United States.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:26.51,2:23:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Twenty minutes after we launch,\Nnone of that will matter!
Dialogue: 0,2:23:29.17,2:23:31.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m inclined to agree\Nwith the President.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:31.34,2:23:34.17,Default,,0,0,0,,While we stand here arguing,\Nthe Entity is preparing to attack, ma’am!
Dialogue: 0,2:23:34.34,2:23:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You may choose to live\Nin the Entity’s reality, gentlemen. I don’t.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:38.39,2:23:39.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold for the President.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:39.96,2:23:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,General Overton’s office,\NStrategic Command.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:42.09,2:23:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,General Overton,\Nthis is the President calling with an unorthodox command.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:46.14,2:23:48.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I need you to listen to my\Ninstructions very carefully
Dialogue: 0,2:23:48.84,2:23:51.19,Default,,0,0,0,,and follow them to the letter\Nwithout hesitation.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:53.58,2:23:55.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[gunshots]\N[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:23:58.63,2:24:00.28,Default,,0,0,0,,[all] Madam President?\NI’m fine. I’m fine.
Dialogue: 0,2:24:16.00,2:24:17.22,Default,,0,0,0,,General!
Dialogue: 0,2:24:19.65,2:24:21.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam President.
Dialogue: 0,2:24:31.01,2:24:33.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[alarm blares]
Dialogue: 0,2:24:50.73,2:24:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,[rumbling]
Dialogue: 0,2:24:57.04,2:24:58.48,Default,,0,0,0,,[clicking, whirring]
Dialogue: 0,2:25:07.44,2:25:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The Entity will be\Nfueling its missiles by now,
Dialogue: 0,2:25:09.70,2:25:11.92,Default,,0,0,0,,but it still needs a place\Nto hide before it launches.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:12.09,2:25:14.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Talk to me, Grace.\NI’ve got it. It’s done.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:14.66,2:25:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Receiver’s connected.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:16.01,2:25:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. Here we go.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:17.40,2:25:18.49,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re gonna switch\Nthe power back on.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:20.10,2:25:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[mechanical clicks, whirring]
Dialogue: 0,2:25:22.06,2:25:23.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Receiver’s activated.\NRed light is on.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:23.67,2:25:25.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Degas, how we doing?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:25:25.19,2:25:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Great. We’re extracting\Nthe last detonator.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:26.76,2:25:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re ready to cut the fuses.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:27.85,2:25:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Four minutes on the clock.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:29.46,2:25:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Understood. Four minutes.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:31.11,2:25:32.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Insert the drive.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:32.90,2:25:34.60,Default,,0,0,0,,[device chimes]\N[Grace] Ready.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:34.77,2:25:36.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Now, you’re gonna watch\Nthe lights on the receiver.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:37.08,2:25:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,When the red light turns--
Dialogue: 0,2:25:40.12,2:25:41.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[groans] What? Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:42.12,2:25:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,When the red light turns green,
Dialogue: 0,2:25:44.17,2:25:47.22,Default,,0,0,0,,you’ll know Ethan has connected\Nthe pill to the Podkova
Dialogue: 0,2:25:47.39,2:25:49.70,Default,,0,0,0,,and the Entity\Nhas been infected with Luther’s algorithm.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:49.87,2:25:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. Then what?
Dialogue: 0,2:25:51.74,2:25:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you’re gonna cut that\Nred wire and let the Entity in.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:56.10,2:25:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,All we need now is\Nfor Ethan to get that pill.
Dialogue: 0,2:25:59.88,2:26:01.53,Default,,0,0,0,,He’ll figure it out.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:34.05,2:26:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[thudding]
Dialogue: 0,2:26:50.50,2:26:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:26:56.11,2:26:57.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:27:04.47,2:27:05.73,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:27:24.05,2:27:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouts]
Dialogue: 0,2:27:26.05,2:27:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,2:27:36.89,2:27:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine whining]
Dialogue: 0,2:28:04.53,2:28:06.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine revs]
Dialogue: 0,2:28:20.89,2:28:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:28:32.60,2:28:34.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[laughs]
Dialogue: 0,2:28:36.78,2:28:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[strains]
Dialogue: 0,2:28:38.69,2:28:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:29:14.16,2:29:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[no audible dialogue]
Dialogue: 0,2:29:22.26,2:29:23.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine sputters]
Dialogue: 0,2:29:32.14,2:29:33.40,Default,,0,0,0,,[grunts]
Dialogue: 0,2:29:50.46,2:29:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[agonized screaming]
Dialogue: 0,2:30:15.53,2:30:17.14,Default,,0,0,0,,[yells]
Dialogue: 0,2:30:25.49,2:30:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,[strained shouts]
Dialogue: 0,2:30:30.24,2:30:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Only one of us has a parachute!
Dialogue: 0,2:30:33.33,2:30:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck! [laughs]
Dialogue: 0,2:30:35.50,2:30:36.50,Default,,0,0,0,,[thuds]
Dialogue: 0,2:30:44.91,2:30:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine whines, stalls]
Dialogue: 0,2:30:56.35,2:30:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[engine sputtering]
Dialogue: 0,2:31:20.55,2:31:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,[Donloe]\NWe’re almost out of time.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:22.33,2:31:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,At 10 seconds I’m gonna\Ncount backwards from three.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:25.08,2:31:27.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Three, two, one, cut.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:27.60,2:31:29.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we run like\Nhell for that door.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:29.52,2:31:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,[Benji] Remember,\Nwhen that drive lights up
Dialogue: 0,2:31:31.73,2:31:33.38,Default,,0,0,0,,you’ll know\Nthe Entity’s inside.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:33.56,2:31:35.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You have 100 milliseconds.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:36.70,2:31:37.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers in French]\NThe blink of an eye.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:40.28,2:32:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you, Ethan?
Dialogue: 0,2:33:05.00,2:33:06.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[gasps] Ethan!
Dialogue: 0,2:33:07.35,2:33:08.66,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,2:33:09.70,2:33:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[rumbling, whirring]
Dialogue: 0,2:33:13.75,2:33:15.67,Default,,0,0,0,,[echoing mechanical thuds]
Dialogue: 0,2:33:35.38,2:33:38.25,Default,,0,0,0,,[breathing shakily]
Dialogue: 0,2:33:57.05,2:33:59.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,2:34:31.04,2:34:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,[telephone ringing]
Dialogue: 0,2:34:39.71,2:34:41.28,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the President.
Dialogue: 0,2:34:42.84,2:34:44.76,Default,,0,0,0,,[exhales shakily]
Dialogue: 0,2:34:47.02,2:34:48.07,Default,,0,0,0,,[sighs]
Dialogue: 0,2:34:52.28,2:34:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,He did it.
Dialogue: 0,2:34:56.90,2:35:00.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That son of a bitch\Nactually did it.
Dialogue: 0,2:35:25.88,2:35:27.32,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther on recording]\N{\i1}Hello, brother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:30.15,2:35:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you’re listening to this,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:32.58,2:35:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the world is still here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:34.80,2:35:36.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And so are you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:37.37,2:35:41.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For the record, {\i0}\N{\i1}I never had a moment of doubt.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:43.03,2:35:46.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew you’d find a way.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:47.38,2:35:49.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You always do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:51.82,2:35:55.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hope in time{\i0}\N{\i1}you can see this life{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:55.30,2:35:58.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}was not some quirk of fate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:35:58.52,2:36:01.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This was your calling.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:01.70,2:36:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your destiny.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:03.75,2:36:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A destiny that touches {\i0}\N{\i1}every living thing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:10.23,2:36:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like it or not, {\i0}\N{\i1}we are masters of our fate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:15.71,2:36:18.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nothing is written.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:21.20,2:36:22.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And our cause,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:23.64,2:36:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}however righteous,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:25.20,2:36:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}pales in comparison{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:27.51,2:36:29.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to the impact{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:29.42,2:36:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of our effect.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:34.56,2:36:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Any hope for a better future{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:37.17,2:36:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}comes from willing{\i0}\N{\i1}that future into being.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:40.61,2:36:46.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A future reflecting the measure {\i0}\N{\i1}of good within ourselves.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:46.40,2:36:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Fire control!
Dialogue: 0,2:36:47.92,2:36:49.97,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther] {\i1}And all that{\i0}\N{\i1}is good inside us...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:50.14,2:36:51.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Stand down.
Dialogue: 0,2:36:51.40,2:36:53.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[Luther]\N{\i1}...is measured by the good{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:53.75,2:36:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}we do for others.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:36:58.97,2:37:01.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We all share the same fate,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:01.54,2:37:03.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the same future.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:03.33,2:37:06.07,Default,,0,0,0,,[shouting indistinctly]
Dialogue: 0,2:37:07.11,2:37:11.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The sum of our{\i0}\N{\i1}infinite choices.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:12.47,2:37:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}One such future is built{\i0}\N{\i1}on kindness, trust{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:16.12,2:37:18.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and mutual understanding...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:22.04,2:37:23.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}should we choose{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:23.56,2:37:25.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to accept it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:28.92,2:37:30.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Driving without question...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:32.75,2:37:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}towards a light we cannot see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:38.80,2:37:41.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not just for those{\i0}\N{\i1}we hold close...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:45.37,2:37:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,[whispers] Hi, Mom.
Dialogue: 0,2:37:46.89,2:37:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}...but for those{\i0}\N{\i1}we’ll never meet.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:53.64,2:37:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hope you know {\i0}\N{\i1}I’ll always love you, brother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:37:58.16,2:38:00.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I will see you again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:38:01.47,2:38:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though I hope{\i0}\N{\i1}it’s not too soon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:38:03.43,2:38:05.39,Default,,0,0,0,,[helicopter blades whirring]
Dialogue: 0,2:38:10.05,2:38:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The world still needs you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:38:13.70,2:38:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course,{\i0}\N{\i1}they’ll never know it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:38:16.01,2:38:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But we do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:38:20.36,2:38:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We who live and die{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:38:23.32,2:38:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in the shadows.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:38:26.80,2:38:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This message will self-destruct {\i0}\N{\i1}in five seconds.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:38:32.85,2:38:34.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good luck, Ethan.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:42:32.26,2:42:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,[ {\i1}Mission: Impossible{\i0}\Ntheme playing]
